1
00:00:04,505 --> 00:00:08,885
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

2
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:00,277
( Dramatic instrumental music )

3
00:01:34,678 --> 00:01:36,851
301A to car 5W , code one .

4
00:01:37,097 --> 00:01:39,020
5W to 301A , go ahead , Johnny .

5
00:01:39,099 --> 00:01:40,601
JOHNNY : We 're chasing wind , Ben .

6
00:01:40,684 --> 00:01:44,939
Maybe the guy who sent in that report drank his breakfast . Let 's call it .

7
00:01:45,647 --> 00:01:47,115
Wait a minute .

8
00:02:09,171 --> 00:02:11,845
JOHNNY : It 's a kid , all right . Maybe 50 yards off the road .

9
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:14,768
I 'll keep circling her until you pick her up .

10
00:02:14,885 --> 00:02:16,728
- 10-10 . - 10-10 .

11
00:02:31,109 --> 00:02:35,364
( Dramatic instrumental music )

12
00:02:42,621 --> 00:02:43,964
BEN : Hey !

13
00:02:44,915 --> 00:02:46,383
Hey , honey !

14
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:50,132
BEN : Hey , little girl . Little girl !

15
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:00,597
Wait a minute . What are you doing out here ?

16
00:03:03,183 --> 00:03:04,230
Honey

17
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,442
what 's your name ?

18
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:13,868
Who do you belong to ?

19
00:03:30,544 --> 00:03:32,421
JOHNNY : Car 5W , code one .

20
00:03:35,966 --> 00:03:38,310
Car 5W to 301A , go ahead .

21
00:03:38,385 --> 00:03:41,389
( Radio crackle and interference )

22
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:42,848
10-9 , Johnny .

23
00:03:43,306 --> 00:03:46,731
JOHNNY : There 's a trailer three miles from you , off the road .

24
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:50,280
I didn 't see anybody around it , you better check it out . 10-10 .

25
00:03:50,439 --> 00:03:52,191
Okay , Johnny . 10-10 .

26
00:03:55,569 --> 00:03:57,321
- What 's the matter with her ? - I don 't know .

27
00:03:57,404 --> 00:03:58,496
ED : Sunstroke ?

28
00:03:58,613 --> 00:04:01,742
BEN : She 's not sunburned . Couldn 't have been in the sun long .

29
00:04:01,825 --> 00:04:03,327
Looks like she 's in shock .

30
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:10,876
Johnny spotted a car and trailer up ahead . Maybe she 's from there .

31
00:04:10,959 --> 00:04:11,755
BEN : Maybe so .

32
00:04:26,850 --> 00:04:31,321
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

33
00:04:46,328 --> 00:04:50,083
ED : No use waking her up unless somebody can identify her . I 'll check it .

34
00:05:15,023 --> 00:05:17,242
- BEN : What is it ? - ED : Have a look .

35
00:05:50,642 --> 00:05:52,736
This blood must be 10 or 12 hours old .

36
00:05:53,937 --> 00:05:57,237
Whatever happened here was either last night or early this morning .

37
00:05:58,942 --> 00:06:00,285
Check outside .

38
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:18,800
( Dramatic instrumental music )

39
00:06:44,571 --> 00:06:46,915
ED : It was sure no traffic accident , was it ?

40
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:50,285
This wasn 't caved in . It was caved out .

41
00:06:50,911 --> 00:06:52,458
Did you find anything ?

42
00:06:52,871 --> 00:06:54,669
No footprints or tire marks .

43
00:06:55,290 --> 00:06:56,507
Found this .

44
00:06:56,833 --> 00:07:00,133
I picked up just one . Six or seven more are scattered over there .

45
00:07:00,211 --> 00:07:01,963
- Sugar . - Yeah .

46
00:07:05,634 --> 00:07:08,012
There 's something over here you should look at .

47
00:07:08,094 --> 00:07:11,098
I don 't know if it 's important , but see what you think .

48
00:07:15,268 --> 00:07:17,646
Mountain lions never come down to the desert .

49
00:07:18,188 --> 00:07:20,691
BEN : No cat ever lived would leave a print like that .

50
00:07:21,024 --> 00:07:22,901
ED : Maybe something was set down there .

51
00:07:22,984 --> 00:07:25,407
A bag , or a can , something like that .

52
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:27,330
It could be almost anything .

53
00:07:29,574 --> 00:07:31,292
I found these inside .

54
00:07:31,743 --> 00:07:35,668
Put in a call for fingerprint and moulage equipment , right away .

55
00:07:35,747 --> 00:07:36,794
ED : Right .

56
00:07:40,085 --> 00:07:43,055
- BEN : Have the medics pick up the kid . - ED : Right .

57
00:07:47,759 --> 00:07:50,638
Car 5W to KMA-628 . Come in , please .

58
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:53,564
RADIO OPERATOR : KMA-628 to car 5W , go ahead .

59
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:56,067
We 're 12 miles north of the crossroads .

60
00:07:56,142 --> 00:07:58,270
Halfway up the secondary road to White Butte .

61
00:07:58,353 --> 00:08:01,277
Station wagon and house trailer with Illinois license plates .

62
00:08:01,356 --> 00:08:04,360
They look pretty well beat up . Looks like a 9-14 .

63
00:08:04,734 --> 00:08:07,237
Picked up a little girl who seems to be in shock .

64
00:08:07,320 --> 00:08:10,415
Send ambulance and medics . We 'll stay here till you arrive .

65
00:08:10,490 --> 00:08:11,912
Anything else ?

66
00:08:12,200 --> 00:08:13,042
ED : Ben ?

67
00:08:14,786 --> 00:08:15,958
10-10 .

68
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:20,759
RADIO OPERATOR : KMA-628 to 5W , location previously reported by 301 - A

69
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,086
will dispatch ambulance .

70
00:08:27,841 --> 00:08:29,593
BEN : Hi , Reggie , how are the kids ?

71
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:32,520
- REGGIE : Fine . Another one on the way . - BEN : Good for you .

72
00:08:43,732 --> 00:08:45,700
- MEDIC : Know what happened to her ? - BEN : No .

73
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:47,573
- MEDIC : Don 't know her name ? - BEN : No .

74
00:08:47,694 --> 00:08:49,537
BEN : Take good care of her .

75
00:08:49,863 --> 00:08:54,084
Give her a nice , easy ride . I 'll be with her all the way to the hospital .

76
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:57,789
( High-pitched stridulation )

77
00:09:18,141 --> 00:09:20,940
( Stridulation fades )

78
00:09:21,019 --> 00:09:22,487
MEDIC : What was that ?

79
00:09:23,146 --> 00:09:24,489
I don 't know .

80
00:09:25,440 --> 00:09:29,195
It must be the wind . It gets pretty freakish in these parts .

81
00:09:30,361 --> 00:09:31,408
Yeah .

82
00:09:31,905 --> 00:09:35,079
BEN : I 'll come soon . I want to be there when she starts talking .

83
00:09:39,329 --> 00:09:43,584
( Wind whistles )

84
00:09:46,961 --> 00:09:48,554
BEN : You know what that is , Cliff ?

85
00:09:48,630 --> 00:09:50,223
I haven 't the faintest idea .

86
00:09:50,298 --> 00:09:54,269
BEN : Hurry before the wind fills it in . Looks like a sandstorm is kicking up .

87
00:09:54,928 --> 00:09:57,397
- You got any idea what happened ? - No .

88
00:09:57,847 --> 00:09:59,724
Nothing that adds up .

89
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,778
How old you figure that kid is ?

90
00:10:07,899 --> 00:10:09,492
Five or six .

91
00:10:10,443 --> 00:10:12,070
Tough break for her .

92
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:14,455
They don 't need us right now .

93
00:10:14,531 --> 00:10:17,626
Let 's go down to Gramps Johnson 's store and see what he knows .

94
00:10:19,119 --> 00:10:22,623
( Wind howls )

95
00:11:02,078 --> 00:11:03,125
BEN : Gramps ?

96
00:11:05,123 --> 00:11:06,500
Gramps !

97
00:11:07,208 --> 00:11:11,679
( Faint radio broadcast )

98
00:11:21,764 --> 00:11:26,019
( Radio becomes louder )

99
00:11:47,123 --> 00:11:48,545
Beats me .

100
00:11:49,626 --> 00:11:51,628
Look , Ed , put in a call ...

101
00:11:53,171 --> 00:11:54,718
Wait a minute .

102
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:28,627
BEN : Gramps .

103
00:12:29,332 --> 00:12:31,835
Looks like he was dragged and thrown down there .

104
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:40,553
( Tense instrumental music )

105
00:12:51,938 --> 00:12:55,238
- BEN : What do you make of it ? - ED : What did you make of the trailer ?

106
00:12:55,483 --> 00:12:59,659
This wasn 't pushed in , it was pulled out . Just like at the trailer .

107
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,411
ED : Ben , have a look at this .

108
00:13:03,408 --> 00:13:04,455
Sugar .

109
00:13:27,307 --> 00:13:29,401
Money wasn 't taken here either .

110
00:13:29,892 --> 00:13:34,489
This is another 9-14 . I 'll call for the guys at the trailer to come .

111
00:13:34,731 --> 00:13:37,280
I want to be at headquarters when the girl talks .

112
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:39,281
ED : I 'll stick around and ride with them .

113
00:13:39,485 --> 00:13:41,704
- Okay . Stay loose . - Sure .

114
00:13:51,998 --> 00:13:54,171
( Switches off radio )

115
00:13:54,250 --> 00:13:59,347
( High-pitched stridulation )

116
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:44,551
( High-pitched stridulation becomes louder )

117
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:52,441
( Gunshots )

118
00:14:52,683 --> 00:14:56,313
( Ed screaming )

119
00:14:56,396 --> 00:14:59,616
( High-pitched stridulation continues )

120
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:06,198
CAPTAIN : With all this , we only know the car and trailer was owned by

121
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,658
a man named Alan Elinson from Chicago .

122
00:15:08,783 --> 00:15:10,285
Yeah , that 's all .

123
00:15:10,535 --> 00:15:14,881
Stop blaming yourself for what happened to Ed Blackburn . It wasn 't your fault .

124
00:15:15,039 --> 00:15:18,168
Somebody had to stay at Johnson 's place , so it happened to be Ed .

125
00:15:18,251 --> 00:15:19,298
Yeah , I know .

126
00:15:19,377 --> 00:15:24,099
We 'll find out who killed him , if he 's dead , along with Gramps and the Elinson family .

127
00:15:24,173 --> 00:15:25,345
So come off it .

128
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:30,268
We 'll get a report on the fingerprints some time this morning . It 'll tell us more .

129
00:15:31,556 --> 00:15:34,275
- Have you figured out what this print is ? - No .

130
00:15:34,684 --> 00:15:35,901
Great .

131
00:15:36,853 --> 00:15:40,403
CAPTAIN : Kit , run down all Gramps ' personal stuff and records .

132
00:15:41,107 --> 00:15:44,611
I don 't think he had an enemy in the world , but somebody might have ...

133
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:46,788
No , wait , that doesn 't make sense .

134
00:15:47,488 --> 00:15:51,538
If somebody wanted to knock off Gramps why tear down half the building to do it ?

135
00:15:53,244 --> 00:15:56,088
I put in a call to check out all the mental institutions .

136
00:15:56,164 --> 00:15:58,713
Everything seems to indicate a homicidal maniac .

137
00:15:59,333 --> 00:16:03,884
There 's no money stolen , violent wreckage . Just sugar taken .

138
00:16:04,255 --> 00:16:06,974
That 's being checked , but it 's a waste of time , too .

139
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:10,429
We 'd have been notified if there was a loony killer on the loose .

140
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:15,650
Gramps got off four shots from his 30-30 before the killer did this to the gun .

141
00:16:16,267 --> 00:16:20,147
And Blackburn was a crack shot . He could hit anything he could see .

142
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:23,282
Unless your maniac was armored like a battleship

143
00:16:23,357 --> 00:16:25,075
there 's no maniac in this case .

144
00:16:25,151 --> 00:16:26,403
Yeah , you 're right .

145
00:16:27,153 --> 00:16:29,497
I want every available man scouting the desert .

146
00:16:29,572 --> 00:16:33,247
If our two planes aren 't enough to cover areas the cars can 't reach

147
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:36,705
I 'll ask permission from the chief to hire a couple more .

148
00:16:37,788 --> 00:16:42,134
Ben , get yourself something to eat and grab some sleep .

149
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:46,056
I don 't want you wearing yourself out so you 'll fold up on us .

150
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:47,924
- BEN : I 've a little score to settle . - CAPTAIN : We all have .

151
00:16:48,674 --> 00:16:51,427
- Report from Washington , Captain . - All right , thanks .

152
00:16:53,054 --> 00:16:55,773
Fingerprints on the trailer check out real good .

153
00:16:55,848 --> 00:17:00,445
Mr. Elinson was an FBI agent on vacation with his wife and two children .

154
00:17:01,270 --> 00:17:04,695
Call the local FBI office . They 've got a stake in this case , now .

155
00:17:05,107 --> 00:17:08,327
Tell them Mr. Elinson 's vacation has been extended indefinitely .

156
00:17:09,570 --> 00:17:11,948
GRAHAM : It 's nice to get off that desert .

157
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:14,955
- It must have been 110 out there today . - At least .

158
00:17:17,411 --> 00:17:18,708
Captain Edwards

159
00:17:18,871 --> 00:17:21,841
this is Robert Graham from the FBI office in Alamogordo .

160
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:24,260
- GRAHAM : How do you do ? - CAPTAIN : Sit down .

161
00:17:24,919 --> 00:17:27,217
Ben here bring you up to date on this business ?

162
00:17:27,296 --> 00:17:30,971
Yes , sir , we went over these exhibits before we left for the desert .

163
00:17:31,050 --> 00:17:34,224
I took him to where we found the trailer and to Johnson 's store .

164
00:17:34,303 --> 00:17:35,896
We 've been there all day . Nothing .

165
00:17:36,055 --> 00:17:37,898
CAPTAIN : Any ideas , Mr. Graham ?

166
00:17:38,015 --> 00:17:39,813
None that make any sense .

167
00:17:39,976 --> 00:17:43,697
I thought you FBI guys were all Quiz Kids , solved everything right away .

168
00:17:44,021 --> 00:17:46,069
I did , too , when I applied for the job .

169
00:17:46,148 --> 00:17:48,321
The planes and cars haven 't found anything .

170
00:17:48,401 --> 00:17:52,406
Give them time . People don 't just drop off the face of the Earth without a trace .

171
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:53,705
We 'll find them .

172
00:17:55,116 --> 00:17:56,789
You know what that is ?

173
00:17:57,368 --> 00:18:00,042
It beats me . Has it been identified yet ?

174
00:18:00,121 --> 00:18:04,922
No , an officer took it to a friend who teaches zoology at the college .

175
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:07,428
He said he 'd never seen anything like it .

176
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:10,677
Lots of evidence , loaded with clues , but nothing adds up .

177
00:18:10,840 --> 00:18:13,810
The Elinson girl is our only real bet . Any news on her ?

178
00:18:13,884 --> 00:18:16,683
No change . I checked with the hospital a half-hour ago .

179
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:20,437
I 'd like to send this to our Washington bureau .

180
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,518
They might be able to identify it .

181
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,236
Or prove that it 's nothing .

182
00:18:24,312 --> 00:18:25,484
All right with me .

183
00:18:25,563 --> 00:18:26,689
( Knocking )

184
00:18:26,772 --> 00:18:27,864
CAPTAIN : Come in .

185
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:30,864
- Hello , Fred . Glad to see you , Ben . - Hi , Doc , how are you ?

186
00:18:30,943 --> 00:18:32,411
You two know each other ?

187
00:18:32,862 --> 00:18:34,159
I don 't believe so .

188
00:18:34,238 --> 00:18:37,492
Dr. Putnam , County Medical Officer . Robert Graham .

189
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:40,624
- He 's with the FBI . Watch your language . - I will .

190
00:18:41,704 --> 00:18:45,254
DOC : I finished the autopsy on Gramps . You want it technical or plain ?

191
00:18:45,333 --> 00:18:47,335
Just plain , Doc . Get to the verb .

192
00:18:47,877 --> 00:18:51,006
Old man Johnson could have died in any one of five ways :

193
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:56,311
His neck and back were broken , his chest crushed , his skull fractured

194
00:18:56,719 --> 00:18:58,721
and here 's one for Sherlock Holmes :

195
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:01,102
There was enough formic acid in him to kill 20 men .

196
00:19:01,766 --> 00:19:03,393
( Dramatic instrumental climax )

197
00:19:15,446 --> 00:19:17,744
I still don 't get this .

198
00:19:18,157 --> 00:19:21,878
Doctors Medford , two of them . Department of Agriculture .

199
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,669
You sent that cast to your outfit in Washington , didn 't you ?

200
00:19:25,748 --> 00:19:26,624
Yeah .

201
00:19:26,707 --> 00:19:29,210
Does this mean that somebody has identified it ?

202
00:19:29,293 --> 00:19:30,510
I don 't know .

203
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,721
- BEN : Great . - AIRMAN : Pardon me , sir .

204
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:35,474
The plane has landed . It 'll load over there .

205
00:19:35,633 --> 00:19:36,680
Thanks .

206
00:19:42,807 --> 00:19:44,275
- GRAHAM : Got a match ? - BEN : Yeah .

207
00:19:44,767 --> 00:19:47,987
( Roaring of plane engine )

208
00:20:17,383 --> 00:20:18,600
Okay , thank you .

209
00:20:21,679 --> 00:20:22,896
GRAHAM : Dr. Medford ?

210
00:20:22,972 --> 00:20:24,645
Are you Dr. Medford ?

211
00:20:24,724 --> 00:20:26,601
Yes , yes . No need to shout .

212
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:30,279
You 're the people . They said you 'd meet us .

213
00:20:30,396 --> 00:20:31,443
BEN : That 's right .

214
00:20:32,022 --> 00:20:33,274
I 'm Bob Graham .

215
00:20:33,357 --> 00:20:35,951
- How do you do ? - This is Sgt. Ben Peterson .

216
00:20:36,819 --> 00:20:39,823
- You 're the one who found the print ? - Yeah , that 's right .

217
00:20:41,365 --> 00:20:42,912
Pat , hurry up .

218
00:20:43,242 --> 00:20:44,585
PAT : I 'm caught .

219
00:20:46,328 --> 00:20:48,877
- OFFICER : Can I help ? - PAT : No , I can manage it .

220
00:20:58,382 --> 00:21:01,135
This is the other Dr. Medford , my daughter , Patricia .

221
00:21:01,218 --> 00:21:03,812
This is the man who found the print . Sergeant ...

222
00:21:03,888 --> 00:21:05,856
- Ben Peterson . - How do you do ?

223
00:21:05,931 --> 00:21:07,899
Then you must be Mr. Robert Graham .

224
00:21:07,975 --> 00:21:09,693
- Yes , how do you do ? - Hello .

225
00:21:09,769 --> 00:21:11,942
We 've got a car to take you to the hotel .

226
00:21:12,021 --> 00:21:13,819
That can wait . We have work to do .

227
00:21:13,898 --> 00:21:16,742
I want to read all your reports right away . Come on , Pat .

228
00:21:16,817 --> 00:21:18,034
PAT : Excuse me , sir .

229
00:21:19,820 --> 00:21:21,743
I should have had this suit pressed .

230
00:21:21,822 --> 00:21:23,620
She 's quite a doctor .

231
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:27,374
If she takes care of sick people , I think I 'll get a fever real quick .

232
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:31,256
GRAHAM : This is where the car and trailer were found .

233
00:21:31,332 --> 00:21:34,051
Twelve miles down this road is the Johnson store .

234
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:35,469
Thank you .

235
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:42,597
Why did the FBI send that print to the Department of Agriculture ?

236
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:45,145
They weren 't able to identify it .

237
00:21:45,805 --> 00:21:49,685
- PAT : You only found one print ? - BEN : That 's right , miss .

238
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:51,189
Have you identified it ?

239
00:21:51,268 --> 00:21:55,114
The Medical Officer 's report on Johnson suggests we were certainly wrong

240
00:21:55,189 --> 00:21:58,693
to even consider this might be a hoax . Read that , Doctor .

241
00:22:00,236 --> 00:22:01,237
Tell me

242
00:22:01,320 --> 00:22:06,497
in what area was the atomic bomb exploded , the first one , back in 1945 ?

243
00:22:06,575 --> 00:22:09,829
Right here in this same general area . White Sands .

244
00:22:14,208 --> 00:22:17,257
1945 . That 's nine years ago .

245
00:22:18,587 --> 00:22:21,010
Genetically , it 's certainly possible .

246
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:26,396
We 're grown up . There 's no need to play footsie with us . We resent it .

247
00:22:26,470 --> 00:22:29,644
If you know what this thing is , Doctor , I suggest you tell us .

248
00:22:29,723 --> 00:22:31,441
We 're assigned to this case , too .

249
00:22:31,517 --> 00:22:35,567
Mr. Graham , we cannot tell you until we 're certain of our theory .

250
00:22:36,063 --> 00:22:40,318
I 'd like to first stop off at the drug store and then see the Elinson girl .

251
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:42,995
She 's still in shock , Doctor . She hasn 't talked yet .

252
00:22:43,070 --> 00:22:47,246
After the girl , I want to examine the territory where you found the print .

253
00:22:54,999 --> 00:22:56,251
You were saying ?

254
00:22:56,417 --> 00:22:59,387
As I explained to Mrs. Johnson , the little girl 's aunt

255
00:22:59,628 --> 00:23:04,805
we hesitate in using a curare to diminish the spasms . She 's too young .

256
00:23:04,884 --> 00:23:09,560
Narcosynthesis would be useless until we overcome the aphonia .

257
00:23:09,763 --> 00:23:12,767
- What 's aphonia ? - Loss of voice .

258
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:16,319
PSYCHIATRIST : She 's a classic case of hysteria conversion .

259
00:23:16,395 --> 00:23:19,114
Only a severe catharsis could jolt her at all .

260
00:23:19,189 --> 00:23:21,237
DR. MEDFORD : May I have a small glass ?

261
00:23:21,609 --> 00:23:25,034
- PSYCHIATRIST : Yes , certainly . - DR . MEDFORD : Pat , that acid we got ...

262
00:23:25,321 --> 00:23:26,163
Acid ?

263
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:29,121
DR. MEDFORD : Formic , Doctor . Thank you .

264
00:23:31,327 --> 00:23:33,705
It may provide the jolt you need .

265
00:23:54,558 --> 00:23:55,605
Them !

266
00:23:56,101 --> 00:23:57,148
Them !

267
00:23:57,645 --> 00:23:58,692
Them !

268
00:23:59,188 --> 00:24:02,408
( Dramatic instrumental music )

269
00:24:07,821 --> 00:24:09,698
May we visit the desert now ?

270
00:24:09,949 --> 00:24:11,496
It 's getting late .

271
00:24:12,034 --> 00:24:13,707
It 's later than you think .

272
00:24:22,753 --> 00:24:27,224
( Dramatic instrumental music )

273
00:24:38,686 --> 00:24:39,733
Thank you .

274
00:24:42,940 --> 00:24:44,192
Quite a breeze .

275
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:47,865
- The goggles , Doctor . - What about them ?

276
00:24:47,945 --> 00:24:50,289
You 're supposed to wear them over your eyes .

277
00:24:50,364 --> 00:24:52,037
Oh , thank you .

278
00:24:53,492 --> 00:24:55,540
Yes , that is better .

279
00:24:57,413 --> 00:25:01,293
- So this is where the car and trailer were ? - Yes , sir . Excuse me .

280
00:25:01,375 --> 00:25:04,424
- Yes , thank you . - The print was found right over there .

281
00:25:06,839 --> 00:25:08,933
BEN : We found it here , by the fire .

282
00:25:09,925 --> 00:25:11,893
You see , there 's nothing there now .

283
00:25:15,556 --> 00:25:17,900
Has there been any report of a strange mound ?

284
00:25:18,058 --> 00:25:21,153
A cone-shaped structure ? Something recently formed ?

285
00:25:21,937 --> 00:25:22,984
No , sir .

286
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:27,489
Sergeant , would you mind if we looked around a little more ?

287
00:25:27,776 --> 00:25:29,494
Anything you say , Doctor .

288
00:25:30,696 --> 00:25:32,698
Rather slim pickings for food , Dad .

289
00:25:32,781 --> 00:25:35,534
They 'd turn carnivorous for lack of a habitual diet .

290
00:25:35,826 --> 00:25:37,294
I believe you 're right .

291
00:25:38,579 --> 00:25:40,297
What would turn carnivorous ?

292
00:25:40,581 --> 00:25:42,629
- PAT : My father will tell you . - GRAHAM : When ?

293
00:25:42,833 --> 00:25:44,961
- When he 's positive . - Now , look , miss ...

294
00:25:45,419 --> 00:25:46,671
Doctor ... .

295
00:25:47,046 --> 00:25:50,095
If the " Doctor " bothers you , why don 't you call me " Pat . "

296
00:25:50,257 --> 00:25:51,383
I 'd like to .

297
00:25:51,592 --> 00:25:54,345
I 've got a job to do , and enough mystery on my hands

298
00:25:54,428 --> 00:25:56,180
without that old ...

299
00:25:57,264 --> 00:25:59,483
I mean , your father complicating things .

300
00:25:59,975 --> 00:26:03,821
He is one of the world 's greatest myrmecologists .

301
00:26:03,937 --> 00:26:07,658
Myrmecologists ! You see , that 's what I mean !

302
00:26:07,900 --> 00:26:11,450
Why don 't we all talk English ? Then we 'd have some understanding .

303
00:26:11,570 --> 00:26:12,617
DR. MEDFORD : Pat !

304
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:15,453
Come here .

305
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:19,332
It 's the same kind of print . Look at it , Doctor .

306
00:26:20,579 --> 00:26:21,922
It 's gigantic .

307
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:27,002
Over 12 centimeters .

308
00:26:27,795 --> 00:26:29,422
That would make the entire- -

309
00:26:29,505 --> 00:26:32,429
About two and a half meters in length . Over 8 feet .

310
00:26:32,841 --> 00:26:34,388
See if there are more .

311
00:26:35,761 --> 00:26:40,358
- This is monstrous . - So is the murder of five people , Doctor .

312
00:26:41,225 --> 00:26:45,651
The direction of that print would indicate it came from that way .

313
00:26:47,940 --> 00:26:52,036
Perhaps we should visit the store . There may be more there now .

314
00:26:52,111 --> 00:26:57,368
Look here , before we do any more visiting , I want to know exactly what this " it " is .

315
00:26:57,449 --> 00:26:59,872
Gentlemen , I understand your impatience .

316
00:26:59,952 --> 00:27:03,673
I know you are concerned with solving what is essentially a local crime

317
00:27:03,747 --> 00:27:06,876
but please believe me , I am not being coy with you .

318
00:27:06,959 --> 00:27:11,430
If I 'm wrong , no harm has been done . But if I 'm correct

319
00:27:11,505 --> 00:27:14,429
and the mounting evidence only fortifies my theory

320
00:27:14,550 --> 00:27:18,145
then something incredible has happened in this desert .

321
00:27:18,220 --> 00:27:22,726
In which case , none of us will dare risk revealing it , because

322
00:27:22,808 --> 00:27:25,231
none of us can risk a nationwide panic .

323
00:27:25,435 --> 00:27:26,652
A Panic ?

324
00:27:44,454 --> 00:27:48,709
( High-pitched stridulation )

325
00:28:34,671 --> 00:28:39,142
( Gunshots )

326
00:28:44,223 --> 00:28:46,897
Get the antennae ! Get the antennae !

327
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:58,495
Get the other antenna !

328
00:28:58,612 --> 00:29:01,741
Get the other antenna ! He 's helpless without them !

329
00:29:16,421 --> 00:29:18,389
( High-pitched stridulation stops )

330
00:29:42,239 --> 00:29:43,707
BEN : What is it ?

331
00:29:43,782 --> 00:29:46,911
Spades appears to be Camponotus vicinus .

332
00:29:48,036 --> 00:29:50,789
Of the family of Formicidae . An ant .

333
00:29:50,872 --> 00:29:54,502
An ant ? I don 't believe it . It 's not possible !

334
00:29:54,876 --> 00:29:58,096
Then this is what got Ed Blackburn , Gramps Johnson , and the rest ?

335
00:29:58,171 --> 00:30:00,765
Yes . A fantastic mutation .

336
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:05,646
Probably caused by lingering radiation from the first atomic bomb .

337
00:30:05,929 --> 00:30:07,021
Notice its odor ?

338
00:30:08,223 --> 00:30:12,353
Formic acid ? That 's why the girl reacted so violently .

339
00:30:12,436 --> 00:30:15,189
The Coroner said that Gramps was filled with it .

340
00:30:15,522 --> 00:30:17,445
DR. MEDFORD : See that ? It 's the stinger .

341
00:30:17,858 --> 00:30:21,488
Ants use their mandibles to rend , tear and hold their victims

342
00:30:21,903 --> 00:30:25,749
but they kill with that , by injecting formic acid .

343
00:30:26,116 --> 00:30:28,210
Mr. Johnson was stung to death .

344
00:30:28,327 --> 00:30:31,331
There 's no time to lose . We must find the colony , the nest .

345
00:30:31,455 --> 00:30:32,707
There 's more of them ?

346
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:35,383
This was probably just a scout , foraging for food .

347
00:30:35,459 --> 00:30:37,632
You heard the sound . The stridulation .

348
00:30:37,711 --> 00:30:39,884
It communicated with others in the colony .

349
00:30:39,963 --> 00:30:42,057
You mean these things send messages ?

350
00:30:42,132 --> 00:30:46,638
Of course . All insects have means of communication with their own kind !

351
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:50,770
( High-pitched stridulation recommences )

352
00:31:00,567 --> 00:31:03,867
We may be witnesses to a Biblical prophesy come true .

353
00:31:06,448 --> 00:31:10,294
" And there shall be destruction and darkness come upon creation .

354
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:12,747
" And the Beasts shall reign over the earth . "

355
00:31:12,829 --> 00:31:15,833
( High-pitched stridulation continues )

356
00:31:33,683 --> 00:31:37,779
Doctor , this nest we 're looking for . How many giant ants will be in it ?

357
00:31:38,271 --> 00:31:39,944
General , I really don 't know .

358
00:31:40,315 --> 00:31:43,865
If they follow the usual pattern of their species , the nest

359
00:31:44,111 --> 00:31:48,992
depending upon its age , may contain hundreds or thousands .

360
00:31:49,658 --> 00:31:51,911
- Thousands , Doctor ? - It 's possible .

361
00:31:52,077 --> 00:31:55,923
Look , if we run into thousands of the thing you killed yesterday

362
00:31:56,164 --> 00:32:00,169
it 'll take a bomber squadron plus an infantry regiment to mop up .

363
00:32:00,252 --> 00:32:01,970
How could we keep that a secret ?

364
00:32:02,045 --> 00:32:04,343
You 're jumping to conclusions , General .

365
00:32:04,464 --> 00:32:07,764
There may not be nearly so many of these creatures as you suppose .

366
00:32:07,843 --> 00:32:11,097
I 'm not supposing anything after looking at that carcass .

367
00:32:11,179 --> 00:32:14,308
What I can 't understand is why no one has seen them until now .

368
00:32:14,391 --> 00:32:18,191
For one reason , I don 't believe these creatures developed until recently .

369
00:32:18,353 --> 00:32:20,697
For another , their being here

370
00:32:20,814 --> 00:32:24,159
in these hundreds of thousands of square miles of desert is ...

371
00:32:29,364 --> 00:32:30,786
No , that isn 't it .

372
00:32:31,908 --> 00:32:35,208
- Could I speak to my daughter , please ? - Of course .

373
00:32:36,496 --> 00:32:37,543
Thank you .

374
00:32:42,210 --> 00:32:43,257
Hello , Pat ?

375
00:32:44,045 --> 00:32:47,219
- DR. MEDFORD : Pat ? You there ? - BEN : That 's not the way to call .

376
00:32:47,507 --> 00:32:49,851
BEN : We 're Search Able , call Search Baker .

377
00:32:50,051 --> 00:32:51,803
- Right , General ? - Right .

378
00:32:53,221 --> 00:32:56,521
Search Able to Search Baker .

379
00:32:56,933 --> 00:32:57,980
Say , " Over . "

380
00:32:58,268 --> 00:32:59,520
Then say , " Over . "

381
00:32:59,603 --> 00:33:00,775
Over !

382
00:33:00,854 --> 00:33:03,858
Medford and Baker to Medford and Able . Go ahead , Dad . Over .

383
00:33:03,940 --> 00:33:05,817
Have you found anything yet ?

384
00:33:06,026 --> 00:33:06,993
Say , " Over . "

385
00:33:07,068 --> 00:33:08,991
- I just said it . - I know . Say it again .

386
00:33:09,070 --> 00:33:10,071
Over !

387
00:33:10,363 --> 00:33:12,206
Baker to Able : Not yet .

388
00:33:12,699 --> 00:33:15,498
We 're about three quarters of the way across our sector .

389
00:33:15,660 --> 00:33:17,879
We 're now at coordinates : Charlie-6 . Over .

390
00:33:17,954 --> 00:33:19,547
DR. MEDFORD : Don 't pass up a thing .

391
00:33:19,623 --> 00:33:22,046
Let me know when you find anything .

392
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:23,798
If you 're finished say , " Over and out . "

393
00:33:23,877 --> 00:33:26,175
- She knows I 'm through talking . - I know she does .

394
00:33:26,254 --> 00:33:28,427
It 's a rule . You 've got to say it . Right , General ?

395
00:33:28,507 --> 00:33:30,555
- GENERAL : Right . - DR . MEDFORD : Ridiculous .

396
00:33:30,842 --> 00:33:33,766
- Lot of good your rules will do- - - Over and out .

397
00:33:33,929 --> 00:33:35,681
Now you 're happy -

398
00:33:36,181 --> 00:33:37,728
( Exasperated sigh )

399
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:41,945
Real calm fellow , isn 't he ?

400
00:33:46,525 --> 00:33:47,993
Worried about him ?

401
00:33:48,109 --> 00:33:52,990
A little . He 's not a young man . He shouldn 't have made this trip , but

402
00:33:53,073 --> 00:33:56,668
he 's a scientist and this is a scientist 's dream come true .

403
00:33:57,410 --> 00:33:59,879
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

404
00:33:59,955 --> 00:34:01,047
PAT : Hold it !

405
00:34:22,310 --> 00:34:24,813
PAT : Fly back over it and get as close as you can .

406
00:34:29,067 --> 00:34:33,322
( High-pitched stridulation )

407
00:34:52,299 --> 00:34:54,643
You 've just found your missing persons .

408
00:34:58,179 --> 00:34:59,726
Look , Dr. Medford

409
00:35:00,015 --> 00:35:03,690
you 're being inconsistent . First , you insist it 's top secret .

410
00:35:04,394 --> 00:35:08,490
Nobody else must know or do anything about getting rid of these big ants .

411
00:35:08,565 --> 00:35:11,284
DR. MEDFORD : Correct . Absolute secrecy is imperative .

412
00:35:11,359 --> 00:35:14,863
But then you turn around and say that time is the most important thing .

413
00:35:14,946 --> 00:35:18,450
I 've been told to take orders from you and give you what you ask for .

414
00:35:18,533 --> 00:35:22,538
But if time is that important , why not let me go in tonight with some bombers

415
00:35:22,621 --> 00:35:23,998
and wipe out that nest ?

416
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:28,551
If you 'll just calm down , General , I 'll explain .

417
00:35:28,960 --> 00:35:31,179
DR. MEDFORD : Doctor , please put up that chart .

418
00:35:31,838 --> 00:35:35,058
Time is important , more so than you realize .

419
00:35:35,133 --> 00:35:38,979
But bombing that nest tonight would only aggravate our problem .

420
00:35:39,346 --> 00:35:42,145
The reason none of them have been seen during the day

421
00:35:42,265 --> 00:35:44,359
even by the police spotting planes

422
00:35:44,434 --> 00:35:47,028
is because they hate the heat of the desert .

423
00:35:47,103 --> 00:35:50,482
They forage between sunset and dawn , when it 's cool .

424
00:35:50,565 --> 00:35:53,569
So half the colony wouldn 't even be inside the nest tonight .

425
00:35:54,152 --> 00:35:59,033
Our best chance will be during the hottest part of the day tomorrow .

426
00:36:02,202 --> 00:36:04,625
DR. MEDFORD : This illustrates a typical ant nest .

427
00:36:05,789 --> 00:36:07,541
Observe the details .

428
00:36:07,957 --> 00:36:09,379
Here is the entrance .

429
00:36:09,709 --> 00:36:13,805
These are tunnels , corridors , and food chambers .

430
00:36:13,963 --> 00:36:16,512
Note the wonderful and intricate engineering .

431
00:36:17,050 --> 00:36:20,099
Water traps , so that none will drown during rains .

432
00:36:20,679 --> 00:36:23,307
This is somewhat oversimplified , I admit

433
00:36:23,390 --> 00:36:26,519
but it will give you an idea of what we are up against .

434
00:36:27,310 --> 00:36:30,860
Do you know that some species of desert ants dig down

435
00:36:31,189 --> 00:36:33,237
as deep as 30 feet or more ?

436
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:36,199
That nest we found today might go down hundreds of feet .

437
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:38,905
We can pinpoint that opening . Seal it up for good .

438
00:36:38,988 --> 00:36:41,537
The creatures would only tunnel out somewhere else .

439
00:36:41,908 --> 00:36:45,037
We don 't want that nest damaged . Not yet .

440
00:36:45,161 --> 00:36:46,333
GRAHAM : What do we do ?

441
00:36:46,413 --> 00:36:49,337
First , we wait until noon tomorrow .

442
00:36:49,416 --> 00:36:52,590
By that time , all of them should be within the nest .

443
00:36:53,169 --> 00:36:55,888
To keep them confined in there is our next problem .

444
00:36:56,589 --> 00:36:58,182
We have two possibilities :

445
00:36:58,258 --> 00:37:00,681
First would be to flood the nest .

446
00:37:00,844 --> 00:37:05,270
Ants will not come through deep water . They breathe through their sides .

447
00:37:05,348 --> 00:37:09,569
Excuse me , Doctor , there 's no water line within 20 miles of that place .

448
00:37:09,644 --> 00:37:12,773
GENERAL : That 's why you asked about our meteorological station .

449
00:37:12,856 --> 00:37:15,075
Any chance of getting cloud formations ?

450
00:37:15,150 --> 00:37:17,494
Nothing that would make cloud seeding pay off .

451
00:37:17,569 --> 00:37:20,743
Nobody 's had any luck in making rain in this part of the desert .

452
00:37:20,822 --> 00:37:22,244
The second possibility ?

453
00:37:22,323 --> 00:37:26,123
Enough heat to drive the ants deeper down into the nest , and hold them down .

454
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:27,920
But no bombing ?

455
00:37:28,121 --> 00:37:31,625
What about phosphorus ? We can lay it over that mound with bazookas .

456
00:37:32,709 --> 00:37:34,882
That would keep the surface area hot .

457
00:37:35,587 --> 00:37:37,385
What happens after that ?

458
00:37:37,464 --> 00:37:40,764
We then drop cyanide gas into the opening and kill them .

459
00:37:41,259 --> 00:37:43,557
How can you be sure you 'll get all of them ?

460
00:37:43,636 --> 00:37:45,354
We go down into the nest and find out .

461
00:37:45,847 --> 00:37:49,897
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

462
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:54,447
( Dramatic instrumental music )

463
00:38:11,372 --> 00:38:14,171
Don 't forget to tap me when you get that wired , General .

464
00:38:14,250 --> 00:38:17,049
Don 't rush me . I 'm doing this by the book .

465
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:23,305
It 's the first time I ever loaded one of these babies .

466
00:38:23,510 --> 00:38:27,606
That makes us even . This is the first time I 've ever given orders to a general .

467
00:39:06,010 --> 00:39:10,265
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

468
00:39:15,228 --> 00:39:17,981
We should 've waited for it to cool more .

469
00:39:18,064 --> 00:39:20,783
We don 't dare lose time getting cyanide into that nest .

470
00:39:42,338 --> 00:39:45,968
( High-pitched stridulation )

471
00:39:59,606 --> 00:40:03,031
( Explosions )

472
00:40:06,571 --> 00:40:07,993
DR. MEDFORD : Marvelously made .

473
00:40:08,239 --> 00:40:11,368
Marvelous . Tell me , you only saw the one live ant ?

474
00:40:11,618 --> 00:40:14,337
He seemed to be trying to get out , rather than get us .

475
00:40:14,495 --> 00:40:17,965
He stopped moving when the gas hit him . Then he dropped out of sight .

476
00:40:18,041 --> 00:40:20,169
Didn 't see or hear a thing from then on .

477
00:40:20,251 --> 00:40:22,003
BEN : You think they 're all dead ?

478
00:40:22,086 --> 00:40:23,963
I think so . You used enough gas .

479
00:40:24,047 --> 00:40:27,347
All parts of the nest should have been thoroughly saturated by now .

480
00:40:27,425 --> 00:40:30,269
If I can still raise an arm when we get out of here

481
00:40:30,345 --> 00:40:32,598
I 'll show you how well saturated I can get .

482
00:40:32,680 --> 00:40:33,897
BEN : I 'm with you .

483
00:40:33,973 --> 00:40:35,725
DR. MEDFORD : If I were younger , I ...

484
00:40:38,269 --> 00:40:39,816
GRAHAM : What are you made up for ?

485
00:40:39,896 --> 00:40:41,819
I 'm going with you and Ben .

486
00:40:43,483 --> 00:40:44,530
No , you 're not .

487
00:40:44,609 --> 00:40:47,078
PAT : Someone with scientific knowledge has to go .

488
00:40:47,445 --> 00:40:50,415
My father is physically unable to do it . That leaves me .

489
00:40:50,490 --> 00:40:54,085
That leaves you here . We don 't know what we 'll find down there .

490
00:40:54,327 --> 00:40:57,456
One thing for sure , it 's no place for you or any other woman .

491
00:40:57,538 --> 00:41:01,543
DR. MEDFORD : She wanted to go , Robert . As a scientist , I couldn 't forbid her .

492
00:41:01,626 --> 00:41:04,095
- PAT : A trained observer has to go . - GRAHAM : What for ?

493
00:41:04,170 --> 00:41:06,923
There are more important things than finding dead ants .

494
00:41:07,006 --> 00:41:09,759
- You wouldn 't know what to look for ! - You tell us what .

495
00:41:09,842 --> 00:41:12,561
There 's no time to give you a course in insect pathology !

496
00:41:12,637 --> 00:41:15,015
So let 's stop talking and get on with it .

497
00:41:20,395 --> 00:41:21,442
Okay .

498
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:24,357
PAT : Don 't worry , Dad .

499
00:41:33,241 --> 00:41:34,538
GRAHAM : Good luck , Sergeant .

500
00:41:34,784 --> 00:41:36,331
GRAHAM : You come last , Pat .

501
00:41:36,869 --> 00:41:39,418
Throw us the rest of the stuff down when I signal .

502
00:41:40,748 --> 00:41:45,003
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

503
00:42:32,508 --> 00:42:33,555
PAT : Hold it .

504
00:42:34,135 --> 00:42:37,435
PAT : They 're dead or they would have attacked us right away .

505
00:42:47,065 --> 00:42:51,320
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

506
00:42:51,861 --> 00:42:54,455
PAT : Look . Held together with saliva .

507
00:42:55,656 --> 00:42:58,705
BEN : Spit is all that 's holding me together right now , too .

508
00:43:29,190 --> 00:43:33,445
( Scraping )

509
00:43:53,131 --> 00:43:57,807
( High-pitched stridulation )

510
00:44:11,440 --> 00:44:13,943
( Stridulation stops )

511
00:44:14,026 --> 00:44:16,120
GRAHAM : How come the gas didn 't kill them ?

512
00:44:16,195 --> 00:44:18,744
PAT : The chamber looked caved in from the bombing .

513
00:44:19,323 --> 00:44:21,872
PAT : Sealed up that way , the gas couldn 't reach them .

514
00:44:21,951 --> 00:44:26,127
GRAHAM : If we run into any more live ones , we 're getting out of here .

515
00:44:26,205 --> 00:44:31,302
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

516
00:44:54,942 --> 00:44:56,239
PAT : This is it !

517
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:59,242
The queen 's chamber , and the eggs .

518
00:45:30,728 --> 00:45:33,607
- PAT : This is what I was afraid of . - GRAHAM : What 's wrong ?

519
00:45:34,065 --> 00:45:35,191
PAT : They 're empty .

520
00:45:35,274 --> 00:45:39,825
- GRAHAM : What came out is dead , right ? - PAT : Not the ones hatched from these !

521
00:45:43,532 --> 00:45:45,660
PAT : Now destroy everything in here . Burn it !

522
00:45:45,743 --> 00:45:48,337
- GRAHAM : What ? - PAT : I said burn it . Burn everything !

523
00:45:48,412 --> 00:45:53,509
( Dramatic instrumental music )

524
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,449
Very strange .

525
00:46:18,317 --> 00:46:19,910
DR. MEDFORD : Most unusual .

526
00:46:20,194 --> 00:46:22,663
PAT : No larvae or pupae in the egg chamber .

527
00:46:22,738 --> 00:46:25,207
PAT : They seemed to hatch directly from the eggs .

528
00:46:25,283 --> 00:46:27,502
PAT : I attribute it to the mutation process .

529
00:46:27,576 --> 00:46:29,544
That 's the logical conclusion .

530
00:46:29,620 --> 00:46:33,750
You feel sure those two have gone ? You found no winged ants ?

531
00:46:34,250 --> 00:46:35,672
PAT : We saw only worker ants .

532
00:46:35,751 --> 00:46:38,379
I don 't get it . You act like it was the end of the world .

533
00:46:38,462 --> 00:46:39,714
It could be .

534
00:46:40,923 --> 00:46:44,268
These two empty egg cases contained queen ants .

535
00:46:44,760 --> 00:46:49,231
Newborn queen ants have wings , so have their consorts , male ants .

536
00:46:50,599 --> 00:46:52,897
- You found no ants with wings ? - Not a one .

537
00:46:53,311 --> 00:46:56,690
The fact is we didn 't destroy this first nest soon enough !

538
00:46:57,690 --> 00:47:02,287
Two young queen ants hatched out , dried their wings and flew away

539
00:47:02,611 --> 00:47:06,582
each with one or more winged males . They 've gone on their wedding flight .

540
00:47:07,199 --> 00:47:11,204
We needn 't worry about the males . They 'll die very quickly , but the queens- -

541
00:47:11,287 --> 00:47:14,416
Doctor , are you telling us there 'll be other nests ?

542
00:47:14,498 --> 00:47:17,672
A single queen can lay thousands of eggs .

543
00:47:18,252 --> 00:47:22,428
From these will hatch dozens of other queens , who may in turn ...

544
00:47:24,342 --> 00:47:25,764
GENERAL : How far can they fly ?

545
00:47:26,844 --> 00:47:29,313
These giants ? I don 't know .

546
00:47:30,556 --> 00:47:34,732
Ordinary queens of the smaller species have very limited flying powers .

547
00:47:35,478 --> 00:47:39,574
They 're dependent mostly on winds and thermal currents to carry them along .

548
00:47:39,690 --> 00:47:43,786
They have been found in the stratosphere . But these giants ...

549
00:47:44,904 --> 00:47:46,622
I don 't know , you guess .

550
00:47:46,697 --> 00:47:48,620
I thought today was the end of them .

551
00:47:48,699 --> 00:47:49,746
No .

552
00:47:50,159 --> 00:47:52,036
We haven 't seen the end of them .

553
00:47:52,328 --> 00:47:56,208
We 've only had a view of the beginning of what may be the end of us .

554
00:47:58,209 --> 00:48:00,553
We 'd better inform Washington , General .

555
00:48:00,628 --> 00:48:04,303
( Dramatic instrumental music )

556
00:48:09,553 --> 00:48:13,808
( indistinct chatter )

557
00:48:18,020 --> 00:48:19,317
OFFICIAL : Sergeant Peterson .

558
00:48:19,563 --> 00:48:21,486
- Sir ? - What about your superiors ?

559
00:48:21,565 --> 00:48:25,195
Do they know these creatures are causing the crimes in your desert ?

560
00:48:25,277 --> 00:48:26,494
No , sir , they don 't .

561
00:48:26,570 --> 00:48:29,699
Gen. O 'Brien and Dr. Medford felt that absolute secrecy

562
00:48:29,782 --> 00:48:32,501
about the existence of the big ants was essential .

563
00:48:32,576 --> 00:48:35,625
Do you also think this extraordinary hush-hush is necessary ?

564
00:48:35,704 --> 00:48:39,880
Yes . I don 't think there 's a police force anywhere that could handle the panic

565
00:48:39,959 --> 00:48:42,337
if people found out these babies were loose .

566
00:48:42,420 --> 00:48:44,673
Gentlemen , I believe we are ready .

567
00:48:45,464 --> 00:48:50,436
Some of you have displayed incredulous attitudes towards our reports and photos .

568
00:48:50,678 --> 00:48:54,308
The rest of you are trying to understand the gravity of our situation

569
00:48:55,099 --> 00:48:58,444
but repeatedly ask how really serious it is .

570
00:48:59,562 --> 00:49:03,317
For your edification , I have prepared a short film

571
00:49:03,899 --> 00:49:08,200
which I hope will give you some idea of the nature of the creatures we face .

572
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:10,243
In a small way , of course .

573
00:49:10,948 --> 00:49:12,916
Robert , please turn out the lights .

574
00:49:19,915 --> 00:49:24,341
DR. MEDFORD : These ants and related species are common to most of America .

575
00:49:24,503 --> 00:49:29,725
In fact , you can find them in backyards , empty lots , and fields

576
00:49:29,800 --> 00:49:32,178
throughout the temperate zones of the world .

577
00:49:32,261 --> 00:49:35,356
They haven 't changed in form or habits

578
00:49:35,681 --> 00:49:37,854
for more than 50 million years .

579
00:49:38,309 --> 00:49:41,108
Here , for instance , is one such specimen

580
00:49:41,187 --> 00:49:45,067
that got himself trapped in amber , which we know is at least that old .

581
00:49:45,816 --> 00:49:48,569
Now we come to some different kind of ants .

582
00:49:49,195 --> 00:49:53,496
The big fellow there , feeding on the smaller , red grease-eaters

583
00:49:54,116 --> 00:49:58,417
is of a savage species called Camponotus vicinus Mayr .

584
00:49:58,621 --> 00:50:00,464
He 's of a desert variety .

585
00:50:00,915 --> 00:50:05,045
Very similar to the giant mutations we found in New Mexico .

586
00:50:06,003 --> 00:50:08,597
There is a side view of a small nest .

587
00:50:09,048 --> 00:50:11,142
Those white objects are ant eggs .

588
00:50:12,384 --> 00:50:15,058
Ants don 't see well at all .

589
00:50:15,721 --> 00:50:20,727
They hear , smell and locate objects with their radar-like antennae .

590
00:50:21,227 --> 00:50:24,902
Only after food or an enemy is located with the antennae

591
00:50:25,356 --> 00:50:27,825
are the savage mandibles put to work .

592
00:50:29,944 --> 00:50:33,073
Now , gentlemen , watch this demonstration of power .

593
00:50:33,322 --> 00:50:36,075
A pebble has blocked the entrance to the nest .

594
00:50:36,575 --> 00:50:39,294
That creature is determined to remove the obstacle .

595
00:50:39,995 --> 00:50:45,001
Note how the mandibles are used to grasp the pebble and pull it aside

596
00:50:45,084 --> 00:50:47,507
with only a slight assist from another ant .

597
00:50:48,337 --> 00:50:51,637
There 's the same pebble on a laboratory scale .

598
00:50:52,174 --> 00:50:55,599
Balancing it , is a dish containing 20 ants .

599
00:50:56,220 --> 00:51:00,441
We 've learned that one of these quarter-inch long insects can lift

600
00:51:00,558 --> 00:51:02,811
20 times its own weight .

601
00:51:03,143 --> 00:51:06,272
That 's equal to one of you lifting a ton and a half or more !

602
00:51:07,189 --> 00:51:10,739
Here are rare shots of a newborn queen and her consorts .

603
00:51:12,736 --> 00:51:17,708
Technically , she should be referred to as a princess , until after the mating flight .

604
00:51:17,992 --> 00:51:21,121
Now there is a close shot of a winged male .

605
00:51:21,787 --> 00:51:25,837
Males are unequipped for survival beyond the mating and die soon after .

606
00:51:26,250 --> 00:51:31,006
The queen flies on , or more precisely , is borne by the winds

607
00:51:31,213 --> 00:51:35,013
until her need prompts her to seek a place to lay eggs .

608
00:51:35,884 --> 00:51:39,309
Does a queen ever fly away from her nest once she 's established it ?

609
00:51:39,471 --> 00:51:42,975
No , never . She loses her wings after the wedding flight .

610
00:51:43,559 --> 00:51:45,277
DR. MEDFORD : See ? One has dropped off .

611
00:51:47,938 --> 00:51:51,283
Now she starts her function of establishing a place

612
00:51:51,734 --> 00:51:54,658
in which to lay her eggs and begin the nest .

613
00:51:54,945 --> 00:51:58,666
Queens live quite a long time . They continue to lay eggs

614
00:51:58,824 --> 00:52:00,576
from the one mating

615
00:52:00,659 --> 00:52:03,503
for from 15 to 17 years .

616
00:52:04,330 --> 00:52:06,128
Here are ants at war .

617
00:52:07,333 --> 00:52:12,715
As you can see , ants are savage , ruthless and courageous fighters .

618
00:52:13,589 --> 00:52:18,641
This fight lasted 72 hours between those two alone .

619
00:52:21,180 --> 00:52:24,309
Ants are the only creatures on Earth other than man

620
00:52:24,516 --> 00:52:25,768
who make war .

621
00:52:26,268 --> 00:52:29,067
They campaign . They are chronic aggressors .

622
00:52:29,229 --> 00:52:32,278
They make slave laborers of the captives they don 't kill .

623
00:52:33,359 --> 00:52:38,115
None of the ants previously seen by man were more than an inch in length .

624
00:52:38,614 --> 00:52:40,708
Most were considerably under that size .

625
00:52:40,783 --> 00:52:46,165
But even the most minute of them have an instinct and talent for industry

626
00:52:46,372 --> 00:52:49,751
social organization and savagery

627
00:52:50,876 --> 00:52:54,722
that makes man look feeble by comparison .

628
00:52:55,130 --> 00:52:57,098
How large were the ants you found ?

629
00:52:57,257 --> 00:53:00,602
DR. MEDFORD : The smallest measured nine feet in body length .

630
00:53:01,011 --> 00:53:03,184
That , gentlemen , is why you are here .

631
00:53:03,806 --> 00:53:05,308
To consider this problem .

632
00:53:05,391 --> 00:53:08,520
And I hope , solve it . Because unless you solve it

633
00:53:08,811 --> 00:53:11,439
unless these queens are located and destroyed

634
00:53:11,647 --> 00:53:14,901
before they 've established thriving colonies and can produce

635
00:53:14,983 --> 00:53:17,657
heaven alone knows how many more queen ants

636
00:53:17,820 --> 00:53:21,996
man , as the dominant species of life on Earth

637
00:53:22,241 --> 00:53:23,959
will probably be extinct

638
00:53:24,993 --> 00:53:28,497
within a year , Doc ?

639
00:53:29,498 --> 00:53:31,421
( sighs )

640
00:53:33,377 --> 00:53:35,755
( Ominous instrumental music )

641
00:53:39,508 --> 00:53:41,727
NEWSMAN : How about some information , Senator ?

642
00:53:41,802 --> 00:53:43,099
SENATOR : Sorry , no comment .

643
00:53:43,178 --> 00:53:45,306
There must be something you can tell us .

644
00:53:45,472 --> 00:53:50,569
All the newswire services , AP , UP , INS , are in there , but nothing 's coming out .

645
00:53:50,894 --> 00:53:53,272
No newsmen are being allowed in there .

646
00:53:53,355 --> 00:53:56,108
What was that mysterious 3 : 00 a.m. meeting about ?

647
00:53:56,191 --> 00:53:58,285
Can 't tell you a thing , boys , sorry .

648
00:54:01,989 --> 00:54:05,914
There are about a million radio receivers installed in there , too .

649
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:07,828
- NEWSMAN 2 : Why ? - NEWSMAN : I don 't know .

650
00:54:35,355 --> 00:54:39,360
Texans . When bigger stories are told , Texans will tell them .

651
00:54:39,443 --> 00:54:42,743
Should fit in with the kind of stuff they 're looking for upstairs .

652
00:54:42,821 --> 00:54:45,119
- Know what 's going on in this building ? - No .

653
00:54:45,199 --> 00:54:47,952
Real " T.S. " stuff . Top Secret .

654
00:54:56,126 --> 00:54:58,754
Okay , we 'll meet you at the airport in 20 minutes .

655
00:55:00,130 --> 00:55:03,259
Says he can have us in Brownsville in less than three hours .

656
00:55:04,968 --> 00:55:06,686
DR. MEDFORD : Good luck , Bob .

657
00:55:18,232 --> 00:55:21,702
They ain 't kidding me . Nobody is . Not you , not anybody .

658
00:55:21,777 --> 00:55:24,621
This isn 't a hospital . This is a loony bin . A nuthouse .

659
00:55:25,447 --> 00:55:28,621
Do you think I 'm crazy ? I don 't care what you think . I 'm not !

660
00:55:28,700 --> 00:55:31,374
I saw those things with my own two eyes !

661
00:55:31,453 --> 00:55:35,503
Do you think anybody could make it up ? A guy would have to be nuts ...

662
00:55:39,545 --> 00:55:42,765
You 're a flyer . You didn 't get that yard sitting on the ground .

663
00:55:42,840 --> 00:55:44,717
You 've seen guys blow their stacks .

664
00:55:45,008 --> 00:55:48,558
Do you think I act and talk like a guy who has lost his marbles ?

665
00:55:48,762 --> 00:55:50,810
Tell us what you saw , Mr. Crotty .

666
00:55:50,889 --> 00:55:54,564
I 've told those head-shrinking doctors four dozen times ! I 'm sick of it .

667
00:55:54,893 --> 00:55:58,739
I tell them and I get laughed at and clucked over .

668
00:56:02,109 --> 00:56:03,907
You promise not to laugh at me ?

669
00:56:04,152 --> 00:56:05,074
Promise .

670
00:56:06,029 --> 00:56:07,076
Okay .

671
00:56:07,739 --> 00:56:11,619
I was flying south from Corpus Christi , heading here , Brownsville .

672
00:56:12,661 --> 00:56:16,837
I turned in from the Gulf , heading for the airport about 20 miles out

673
00:56:17,040 --> 00:56:20,840
all of a sudden I see these flying saucers .

674
00:56:20,919 --> 00:56:23,342
Three of them . One big and two little ones .

675
00:56:23,714 --> 00:56:26,843
I had to do some fancy flying or they 'd have run right into me .

676
00:56:26,925 --> 00:56:31,396
I dived down and landed in the first place I saw , a street .

677
00:56:31,805 --> 00:56:33,853
I 've never been so rattled in my life .

678
00:56:34,641 --> 00:56:36,484
I cracked up a little , sure .

679
00:56:36,685 --> 00:56:39,859
I plowed into an old Ford and ended up on someone 's porch .

680
00:56:40,647 --> 00:56:43,776
Who wouldn 't lose their head after seeing something like that ?

681
00:56:43,859 --> 00:56:47,113
- They were flying saucers ? - I don 't know what else to call them .

682
00:56:47,529 --> 00:56:49,497
CROTTY : They were shaped

683
00:56:50,991 --> 00:56:52,413
like ants .

684
00:56:56,663 --> 00:56:59,507
It sounds crazy but that 's what they were shaped like .

685
00:56:59,708 --> 00:57:04,134
The big one was about 15 feet long and had wings like a fly .

686
00:57:04,504 --> 00:57:08,725
The other two seemed to be chasing the big one . One here . Two here .

687
00:57:09,009 --> 00:57:13,355
They zoomed around me like kamikazes . Scared me out of my pants !

688
00:57:13,931 --> 00:57:15,353
Excuse me , ma 'am .

689
00:57:16,141 --> 00:57:19,771
They said that Ford wasn 't a new one . It was all beat up to begin with .

690
00:57:19,937 --> 00:57:21,905
So what 's all the beef ?

691
00:57:24,858 --> 00:57:26,986
You don 't believe me either . Do you ?

692
00:57:27,069 --> 00:57:28,446
On the contrary , we do .

693
00:57:28,528 --> 00:57:29,575
You do ?

694
00:57:30,364 --> 00:57:31,206
Good .

695
00:57:31,448 --> 00:57:35,999
What direction were these flying saucers going the last time you saw them ?

696
00:57:36,453 --> 00:57:39,878
West , I 'd say . Yes , due west .

697
00:57:40,499 --> 00:57:42,376
Will you get me out of here ?

698
00:57:42,584 --> 00:57:45,588
- We 'll speak to the doctor about it . - I 'd appreciate it .

699
00:57:45,671 --> 00:57:49,426
Try and get my clothes , too . They only gave me these slippers

700
00:57:50,050 --> 00:57:52,599
but not even a rope to hold up my pants .

701
00:57:52,719 --> 00:57:55,973
- We 'll be seeing you . - Be right neighborly if you could help .

702
00:57:56,056 --> 00:57:57,524
I 'll sure be hoping .

703
00:57:58,100 --> 00:58:00,228
- DOCTOR : Mr. Graham ? - GRAHAM : Yes ?

704
00:58:00,310 --> 00:58:02,813
How was your talk with Mr. Crotty ?

705
00:58:03,105 --> 00:58:05,324
You 're wise to keep him locked up , Doctor .

706
00:58:05,440 --> 00:58:09,240
I 've recommended his release . He 's not demented .

707
00:58:09,569 --> 00:58:13,324
I 'm convinced he 's trying to pull a publicity stunt with this weird story .

708
00:58:13,407 --> 00:58:15,375
The government wants him to be kept here

709
00:58:15,450 --> 00:58:17,077
so he doesn 't get any publicity .

710
00:58:17,244 --> 00:58:18,336
The government ?

711
00:58:18,453 --> 00:58:20,330
He 's to have no visitors .

712
00:58:20,414 --> 00:58:24,135
If any information is given out about him , you 'll be held responsible .

713
00:58:24,584 --> 00:58:26,837
GRAHAM : I can 't tell you why this is essential .

714
00:58:27,212 --> 00:58:30,386
We 'll let you know as soon as possible . We 'll tell you when he 's well .

715
00:58:36,388 --> 00:58:40,814
A bit more than 700 air miles from White Sands to Brownsville .

716
00:58:41,435 --> 00:58:42,482
Southeast .

717
00:58:42,978 --> 00:58:45,822
This Crotty said they were heading west when he saw them .

718
00:58:45,897 --> 00:58:46,898
I believe him .

719
00:58:46,982 --> 00:58:51,863
There were strong easterly winds the day Crotty saw the ants .

720
00:58:52,154 --> 00:58:54,623
They 'd follow the line of least resistance .

721
00:58:54,865 --> 00:58:59,166
We can surmise that one of the queens , possibly both of them

722
00:58:59,578 --> 00:59:02,923
can create nests in this general area .

723
00:59:04,041 --> 00:59:06,339
We 'd better inform the Mexican authorities

724
00:59:06,501 --> 00:59:09,300
and concentrate our search efforts here .

725
00:59:09,755 --> 00:59:13,385
As far south as Panama . As far north as

726
00:59:14,342 --> 00:59:17,391
Santa Barbara , on the California coast .

727
00:59:17,637 --> 00:59:19,059
That 's an awful lot of area .

728
00:59:19,139 --> 00:59:20,356
( Telephone rings )

729
00:59:20,432 --> 00:59:21,479
I 'll get it .

730
00:59:23,435 --> 00:59:24,482
Hello ?

731
00:59:25,062 --> 00:59:26,939
Dr. Medford speaking .

732
00:59:28,607 --> 00:59:29,733
What ?

733
00:59:30,400 --> 00:59:31,993
I 'll be right there .

734
00:59:32,069 --> 00:59:36,540
( Dramatic instrumental music )

735
00:59:41,953 --> 00:59:45,423
" A nest hatched aboard a ship at sea . "

736
00:59:45,499 --> 00:59:49,754
( Dramatic instrumental music swells )

737
00:59:50,253 --> 00:59:52,005
( Beeping in Morse code )

738
00:59:52,089 --> 00:59:56,560
( Gunshots )

739
00:59:56,843 --> 01:00:00,473
( Screaming )

740
01:00:00,555 --> 01:00:03,559
( High-pitched stridulation )

741
01:00:06,144 --> 01:00:09,865
ADMIRAL : I 'm sure you 'll be interested in this report I just received :

742
01:00:09,940 --> 01:00:13,945
" U.S.S. Milwaukee got radio bearing on S.S. Viking before signal stopped .

743
01:00:14,820 --> 01:00:17,414
" Milwaukee proceeded at once to location .

744
01:00:17,614 --> 01:00:20,538
" Two seamen from Viking rescued from sea by Milwaukee .

745
01:00:21,201 --> 01:00:23,704
" Seamen said no survivors remained aboard Viking .

746
01:00:24,412 --> 01:00:27,086
" Not possible to put aboard search and rescue party ...

747
01:00:27,165 --> 01:00:29,759
" ... as Viking was infested with the giant ants . "

748
01:00:29,835 --> 01:00:34,966
Upon my orders , the 8.8 . Viking has been sunk with naval gunfire .

749
01:00:35,298 --> 01:00:37,767
This was accomplished at 0700 this morning .

750
01:00:37,968 --> 01:00:40,517
I don 't see how a ship at sea could ...

751
01:00:41,263 --> 01:00:42,810
1st OFFICIAL : Dr. Medford

752
01:00:42,889 --> 01:00:46,189
how could these giant creatures get aboard that vessel unseen ?

753
01:00:46,935 --> 01:00:51,111
The S.S. Viking anchored in Acapulco , Mexico , for three days and four nights .

754
01:00:52,357 --> 01:00:56,658
It 's then and there we believe one of these missing queen ants flew aboard .

755
01:00:57,362 --> 01:00:59,330
Please give them your information .

756
01:01:01,575 --> 01:01:04,454
" Owners of the 8.8 . Viking reported that on hold number one ...

757
01:01:04,578 --> 01:01:08,549
" ... the hatch cover was off during the entire time of loading . Even at night .

758
01:01:08,915 --> 01:01:13,011
" The crew had shore leave every night so only a skeleton crew remained on watch . "

759
01:01:13,837 --> 01:01:17,717
It was quite possible for a queen ant to have flown onto that ship unseen .

760
01:01:18,049 --> 01:01:21,974
An open hold would be inviting as a place to lay her eggs and hatch out a nest .

761
01:01:22,470 --> 01:01:27,192
I think it 's time to inform the public . It can 't be kept a secret indefinitely .

762
01:01:27,267 --> 01:01:28,644
We can 't risk it , sir .

763
01:01:28,727 --> 01:01:30,195
But you already have .

764
01:01:30,562 --> 01:01:34,112
The entire crew of the cruiser Milwaukee knows about these things now .

765
01:01:34,191 --> 01:01:38,196
They know , but the Milwaukee will be kept at sea until this is resolved .

766
01:01:39,988 --> 01:01:42,537
What do those flags on the map indicate ?

767
01:01:43,200 --> 01:01:47,080
These four indicate where we found dead male ants .

768
01:01:48,163 --> 01:01:52,589
The most recent finding was about four days ago near Mt . Wilson in California .

769
01:01:53,376 --> 01:01:57,597
It was decomposed and must have been there for a month to five weeks .

770
01:01:58,423 --> 01:02:01,973
This flag , at Los Angeles , indicates a lead .

771
01:02:02,177 --> 01:02:05,021
Mr. Graham and Sgt. Ben Peterson are there now .

772
01:02:05,138 --> 01:02:08,984
They were flown there by Maj. Kibbee to check on a large sugar theft .

773
01:02:09,100 --> 01:02:10,397
Forty tons , to be exact .

774
01:02:13,605 --> 01:02:16,404
( Train whistle blows )

775
01:02:28,745 --> 01:02:30,668
GRAHAM : When was this car broken into ?

776
01:02:30,747 --> 01:02:32,624
I told you , Friday night .

777
01:02:32,916 --> 01:02:36,045
Yard watchman claims he didn 't see or hear a thing .

778
01:02:36,503 --> 01:02:38,676
What 's so important you got to work on Sunday ?

779
01:02:38,755 --> 01:02:40,007
Where 's the watchman ?

780
01:02:40,090 --> 01:02:44,391
City jail . Any boob knows you need trucks to carry away 40 tons of stuff .

781
01:02:44,552 --> 01:02:47,431
Said he didn 't hear them . He 's either lying or he 's deaf .

782
01:02:47,514 --> 01:02:48,731
And he ain 't deaf .

783
01:02:49,724 --> 01:02:51,476
- GRAHAM : Let 's go see him . - BEN : Yeah .

784
01:02:52,936 --> 01:02:54,404
Thanks , buddy .

785
01:02:54,479 --> 01:02:57,232
After spoiling my day off you could at least tell me

786
01:02:57,315 --> 01:02:59,989
how come a government cop is so interested in this deal .

787
01:03:00,068 --> 01:03:01,786
He 's got a sweet tooth .

788
01:03:06,157 --> 01:03:08,501
GRAHAM : It 's the only job you 've ever had ?

789
01:03:08,660 --> 01:03:11,789
I 've had a clean record for 30 years at the railroad .

790
01:03:11,913 --> 01:03:15,543
Yard cop thinks you made a deal not to see that car broken into .

791
01:03:15,625 --> 01:03:17,127
What sense does that make ?

792
01:03:17,210 --> 01:03:19,884
Is sugar rare cargo ? ls there a black market for it ?

793
01:03:19,963 --> 01:03:22,591
Did you ever hear of a fence for hot sugar ?

794
01:03:23,049 --> 01:03:26,553
If I made a deal with crooks , it wouldn 't be for 40 tons of sugar !

795
01:03:26,720 --> 01:03:29,519
I swear I didn 't hear a thing Friday night .

796
01:03:29,764 --> 01:03:31,232
BEN : I 'll be right back .

797
01:03:31,308 --> 01:03:32,855
( Woman crying )

798
01:03:35,270 --> 01:03:39,491
That woman just identified the body of her husband . See him right away .

799
01:03:39,607 --> 01:03:43,157
WATCHMAN : I 've never had anything to do with crooks . I 'm an honest man .

800
01:03:43,236 --> 01:03:46,331
Sure , you can go home now . Take care of him , will you ?

801
01:03:46,573 --> 01:03:47,415
Thank you .

802
01:03:48,575 --> 01:03:50,919
I don 't think this happened in a machine .

803
01:03:51,119 --> 01:03:54,794
Any machine that pulled hard enough to tear his arm off at the shoulder

804
01:03:54,873 --> 01:03:56,967
would also have chopped up his face .

805
01:03:57,250 --> 01:03:59,548
Look at the laceration across his chest .

806
01:04:00,128 --> 01:04:03,223
Can 't figure it , except he died from shock and loss of blood .

807
01:04:03,298 --> 01:04:04,720
Thanks very much .

808
01:04:09,012 --> 01:04:10,389
His name 's Thomas Lodge .

809
01:04:10,472 --> 01:04:14,318
Police found him , 6 : 30 a.m. His car jumped a curb , went into a sign

810
01:04:14,392 --> 01:04:18,147
but not hard enough to do that . They couldn 't find the other arm .

811
01:04:18,646 --> 01:04:21,866
His wife said that he left the house at 5 : 45 .

812
01:04:22,108 --> 01:04:25,578
He had his two kids with him . No sign of the kids yet .

813
01:04:27,155 --> 01:04:29,078
( Melancholic instrumental music )

814
01:04:30,283 --> 01:04:31,626
GRAHAM : Mrs. Lodge

815
01:04:31,701 --> 01:04:35,046
was your husband accustomed to taking his boys out so early ?

816
01:04:35,580 --> 01:04:40,427
Tom works on Sunday from 9 : 00 to 7 : 00 . It 's an extra job he had .

817
01:04:41,127 --> 01:04:44,722
He works so hard , he doesn 't have much time to spend with Jerry and Mike .

818
01:04:44,798 --> 01:04:48,894
Sundays they get up early and go somewhere together to play .

819
01:04:50,387 --> 01:04:53,106
Do you know where they might have gone this morning ?

820
01:04:53,264 --> 01:04:54,311
Where ?

821
01:04:55,266 --> 01:04:57,360
They go different places .

822
01:04:58,395 --> 01:05:00,648
Last Sunday , Tom took the boys to the zoo .

823
01:05:01,439 --> 01:05:03,157
They had such a good time .

824
01:05:03,441 --> 01:05:06,160
Tom fixed it with a keeper so they could get in early

825
01:05:06,236 --> 01:05:08,330
and watch the feeding of the animals .

826
01:05:08,405 --> 01:05:10,248
Jerry talked about it all week .

827
01:05:11,408 --> 01:05:13,001
Where else did they go ?

828
01:05:15,161 --> 01:05:19,041
Sometimes Tom took them boat riding at MacArthur Park .

829
01:05:19,124 --> 01:05:22,219
For pony rides and miniature golf .

830
01:05:23,086 --> 01:05:26,306
They always come home so happy . And so dirty !

831
01:05:26,798 --> 01:05:30,928
I kept asking Tom to do things where they won 't get so dirty .

832
01:05:31,010 --> 01:05:33,263
I spent the rest of the day cleaning them .

833
01:05:53,199 --> 01:05:54,997
Can I see you a moment ?

834
01:06:01,583 --> 01:06:03,130
- BEN : Rough ? - GRAHAM : Yeah .

835
01:06:03,501 --> 01:06:07,096
BEN : Bob , these are the two officers who found Lodge .

836
01:06:07,213 --> 01:06:08,760
- This is Ryan . - Sutton .

837
01:06:08,965 --> 01:06:12,139
Patrolmen Sutton and Ryan . This is Bob Graham .

838
01:06:12,760 --> 01:06:16,560
Dr. Medford and Pat are flying here with Gen. O 'Brien tonight .

839
01:06:16,848 --> 01:06:20,022
Kibbee called . He 'll be over after he 's had a little breakfast .

840
01:06:20,101 --> 01:06:23,230
Show me on the map just exactly where you found Lodge .

841
01:06:24,606 --> 01:06:27,735
- Right there . - And he was dead when you found him ?

842
01:06:28,234 --> 01:06:29,907
Where 's MacArthur Park ?

843
01:06:32,530 --> 01:06:34,077
That 's a long ways .

844
01:06:34,991 --> 01:06:37,494
GRAHAM : We 've got to find out where he took the kids .

845
01:06:37,577 --> 01:06:39,921
He couldn 't have driven far . He was too cut up .

846
01:06:41,247 --> 01:06:44,877
Is there any area where you found him where he might 've taken the kids

847
01:06:44,959 --> 01:06:48,509
for a boat ride or miniature golf ? Pony rides , stuff like that .

848
01:06:48,630 --> 01:06:50,883
RYAN : I don 't know any miniature golf courses .

849
01:06:50,965 --> 01:06:53,593
Griffith Park is the closest where they rent horses .

850
01:06:53,676 --> 01:06:58,022
That 's a long way , too . Doesn 't his wife know where they went ?

851
01:06:58,598 --> 01:06:59,770
No .

852
01:07:00,350 --> 01:07:04,400
Did you make any arrests this morning , say between 4 : 00 a.m. and noon ?

853
01:07:04,562 --> 01:07:05,609
RYAN : Yes , sir .

854
01:07:06,606 --> 01:07:09,029
Four . Three drunks and a traffic citation .

855
01:07:10,527 --> 01:07:12,325
GRAHAM : I 'd like to talk to them .

856
01:07:12,445 --> 01:07:15,369
They might have seen something that 'll help us .

857
01:07:19,827 --> 01:07:21,795
Where were you going when you were arrested ?

858
01:07:21,871 --> 01:07:22,872
I don 't know .

859
01:07:22,956 --> 01:07:25,300
I don 't even know where I was coming from .

860
01:07:26,084 --> 01:07:28,633
- How about you ? - I don 't know either .

861
01:07:32,632 --> 01:07:36,637
As I said before , I prefer the informal type of social life .

862
01:07:37,011 --> 01:07:39,935
- I disagree with you . - Really ?

863
01:07:40,056 --> 01:07:42,275
I 'm at my best in my white tie and tails .

864
01:07:42,350 --> 01:07:45,069
All right , Beau Brummell , knock it off .

865
01:07:45,144 --> 01:07:46,270
Look , miss ...

866
01:07:46,354 --> 01:07:49,358
- All I did was go through a red light . - At 60 mph ?

867
01:07:49,524 --> 01:07:52,573
- Was something chasing you ? - No , I was in a hurry to get home .

868
01:07:52,652 --> 01:07:53,699
Where from ?

869
01:07:53,903 --> 01:07:56,782
I spent the night with a sick friend .

870
01:07:57,407 --> 01:08:00,286
I 'd rather not mention any names , he 's married .

871
01:08:01,452 --> 01:08:03,125
- Okay , you can go . - Thank you .

872
01:08:05,582 --> 01:08:09,086
I 'm through with them . Let them go back to the tank and sleep it off .

873
01:08:09,168 --> 01:08:11,796
- All right , let 's go . - With pleasure , sir .

874
01:08:14,090 --> 01:08:15,933
GRAHAM : You said there were three ?

875
01:08:16,009 --> 01:08:18,728
The other one 's in the alcoholic ward at the hospital .

876
01:08:18,803 --> 01:08:21,101
Practically a permanent resident there .

877
01:08:21,264 --> 01:08:22,811
GRAHAM : Let 's go talk to him , too .

878
01:08:25,727 --> 01:08:28,446
Sneaked out of here Saturday afternoon . Back at 5 : 00 this morning .

879
01:08:28,521 --> 01:08:32,025
You can talk to him , but I don 't think he 'll cooperate .

880
01:08:32,108 --> 01:08:34,202
Hey , Admiral , are we gonna be drafted ?

881
01:08:34,444 --> 01:08:35,491
No , sir .

882
01:08:35,570 --> 01:08:39,495
DOCTOR : Behave yourself , Harry . This is the man . Mind your manners .

883
01:08:39,782 --> 01:08:43,036
- If he gives you trouble , I 'm outside . - He won 't .

884
01:08:43,119 --> 01:08:45,121
BEN : Hello , Jensen . How are you ?

885
01:08:45,288 --> 01:08:49,043
How do , gentlemen ? Looking for recruits ?

886
01:08:49,125 --> 01:08:50,377
KIBBEE : Not today .

887
01:08:50,585 --> 01:08:53,509
- Jensen , you come here often , don 't you ? - I like it here .

888
01:08:53,588 --> 01:08:56,592
- What have you been doing lately ? - Same as always , nothing .

889
01:08:56,674 --> 01:08:58,176
But I got some deals on .

890
01:08:58,259 --> 01:08:59,806
GRAHAM : Sure .

891
01:08:59,969 --> 01:09:03,394
You didn 't see anything unusual yesterday or this morning , did you ?

892
01:09:03,556 --> 01:09:06,685
No , nothing unusual . Same as always .

893
01:09:07,685 --> 01:09:09,187
They 're gone now .

894
01:09:10,021 --> 01:09:12,524
I saw some little airplanes this morning .

895
01:09:13,524 --> 01:09:15,777
Didn 't seem big enough for them to get into .

896
01:09:16,110 --> 01:09:17,453
Big enough for who ?

897
01:09:17,695 --> 01:09:19,117
The ants .

898
01:09:19,572 --> 01:09:22,917
I 'd like to get out of here , but I ain 't joining the Army to do it !

899
01:09:23,034 --> 01:09:25,332
- You can 't make me , there 's laws ! - We know .

900
01:09:25,411 --> 01:09:27,960
Jensen , what kind of ants did you see ?

901
01:09:28,289 --> 01:09:29,711
Big ones .

902
01:09:30,708 --> 01:09:32,255
Ain 't there now .

903
01:09:32,585 --> 01:09:34,929
- Mostly at night I see them . - Where ?

904
01:09:35,421 --> 01:09:38,300
General , I 'll make a deal with you :

905
01:09:38,383 --> 01:09:41,683
If you make me a sergeant in charge of the booze , and I 'll enlist .

906
01:09:41,761 --> 01:09:46,562
Make me a sergeant in charge of the booze !

907
01:09:46,641 --> 01:09:49,770
- Exactly where do these ants show up ? - In the river .

908
01:09:50,144 --> 01:09:51,521
In the river .

909
01:09:52,188 --> 01:09:54,862
I saw it once when it had water in it .

910
01:09:55,233 --> 01:09:56,951
Now , when was that ?

911
01:09:57,819 --> 01:09:59,287
JENSEN : Let me see .

912
01:10:01,447 --> 01:10:02,699
GRAHAM : In the river bed .

913
01:10:02,990 --> 01:10:06,836
Those big openings in the sides are like sewer outlets .

914
01:10:08,371 --> 01:10:11,045
Jensen , how long have you been seeing these things ?

915
01:10:11,124 --> 01:10:14,594
A long time . How long have I been here ?

916
01:10:15,378 --> 01:10:18,097
The doctor says he was first admitted five months ago .

917
01:10:18,172 --> 01:10:19,845
Thanks , Mac .

918
01:10:20,258 --> 01:10:23,387
Take me with you and I 'll enlist , I promise .

919
01:10:23,469 --> 01:10:24,766
Make me a sergeant !

920
01:10:24,887 --> 01:10:28,232
JENSEN : Give me the booze ! Make me a sergeant . Give me the booze !

921
01:10:30,435 --> 01:10:33,188
Please , my nerves !

922
01:10:36,649 --> 01:10:41,075
( Dramatic instrumental music )

923
01:11:08,931 --> 01:11:10,854
Which way is the hospital , Ryan ?

924
01:11:11,768 --> 01:11:13,486
RYAN : Right over there .

925
01:11:24,030 --> 01:11:25,748
Ben , come here .

926
01:11:33,956 --> 01:11:36,800
Pretty good model of a kid 's idea of an L-1 .

927
01:11:37,293 --> 01:11:40,217
Get on the radio and contact Mrs. Lodge .

928
01:11:40,296 --> 01:11:43,800
Find out if the kids ever owned a plane like that . Wait for a report .

929
01:11:43,883 --> 01:11:45,100
RYAN : Right .

930
01:12:14,872 --> 01:12:16,590
Here 's tire marks .

931
01:12:20,920 --> 01:12:24,470
New tires . Lodge had new tires on his car , didn 't he ?

932
01:12:24,757 --> 01:12:25,804
Yeah .

933
01:12:27,260 --> 01:12:28,637
KIBBEE : Hey , Bob ! Ben !

934
01:12:41,482 --> 01:12:43,655
( Dramatic instrumental surge )

935
01:12:43,734 --> 01:12:45,577
BEN : It 's them all right .

936
01:12:45,653 --> 01:12:49,908
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

937
01:12:55,997 --> 01:12:57,999
I don 't smell formic acid , do you ?

938
01:12:58,082 --> 01:13:00,676
No , but it could all fall right into place .

939
01:13:01,168 --> 01:13:04,217
Lodge and his kids down here flying their model plane .

940
01:13:04,297 --> 01:13:06,345
Suddenly , the ants attack .

941
01:13:06,549 --> 01:13:08,802
Lodge fights to protect his kids .

942
01:13:09,510 --> 01:13:12,389
Somehow , he breaks away , gets into his car , and drives off .

943
01:13:13,723 --> 01:13:15,600
But what about the kids ?

944
01:13:15,725 --> 01:13:17,147
Maybe they ran away .

945
01:13:17,435 --> 01:13:19,278
No , we 'd have picked them up by now .

946
01:13:20,605 --> 01:13:22,699
Unless they ran in here .

947
01:13:23,816 --> 01:13:24,863
RYAN : Mr. Graham !

948
01:13:25,776 --> 01:13:28,245
That model plane belonged to the Lodge kids .

949
01:13:28,321 --> 01:13:31,495
The husband used to bring the boys down here to fly it .

950
01:13:31,782 --> 01:13:35,958
Got to be the same plane , same color . And there 's no model plane at home .

951
01:13:36,454 --> 01:13:39,583
Where do these things go ? I mean , how far do they go ?

952
01:13:39,999 --> 01:13:44,004
Don 't know for sure , but there 's more than 700 miles of them under the city .

953
01:13:51,636 --> 01:13:54,435
( Dramatic instrumental music )

954
01:13:54,931 --> 01:13:58,561
( Excited chatter )

955
01:13:59,769 --> 01:14:02,238
NEWSMAN : Why is the Army sending troops into L.A. ?

956
01:14:02,313 --> 01:14:04,281
NEWSMAN 2 : And a Marine regiment ?

957
01:14:04,357 --> 01:14:07,361
NEWSMAN 3 : Why a special press conference at 5 : 00 on a Sunday ?

958
01:14:07,443 --> 01:14:10,413
- You 'll just have to wait . - Why all the VIPs from Washington ?

959
01:14:10,488 --> 01:14:12,206
Has the cold war gotten hot ?

960
01:14:12,281 --> 01:14:14,375
Gentlemen , come in now .

961
01:14:19,664 --> 01:14:24,090
This is the most serious crisis this city has ever faced .

962
01:14:24,251 --> 01:14:26,754
There 's no time for questions . Listen carefully

963
01:14:26,837 --> 01:14:29,716
so you can report the facts to your newspapers .

964
01:14:29,924 --> 01:14:33,269
This is Dr. Harold Medford of the Department of Agriculture .

965
01:14:33,344 --> 01:14:36,268
Gen. O 'Brien , Air Force Intelligence .

966
01:14:36,555 --> 01:14:40,230
Gen. James , Army Intelligence . The others you know .

967
01:14:40,768 --> 01:14:42,441
- Ready , sir ? - One moment .

968
01:14:43,896 --> 01:14:46,024
- ANNOUNCER : Set , Charlie ? - CHARLIE : You 're on .

969
01:14:46,107 --> 01:14:50,112
We interrupt all radio and television programs indefinitely .

970
01:14:50,486 --> 01:14:55,458
Keep your radio and television sets turned on . This is an emergency .

971
01:14:55,533 --> 01:14:58,332
I repeat , this is an emergency !

972
01:14:59,620 --> 01:15:02,590
" By direction of the President of the United States ...

973
01:15:02,748 --> 01:15:06,628
" ... and the Governor of the State of California , and the Mayor ...

974
01:15:07,086 --> 01:15:09,180
" ... the city of Los Angeles is ...

975
01:15:09,505 --> 01:15:13,760
" ... in the interests of public safety , hereby under martial law .

976
01:15:13,843 --> 01:15:17,473
( Exclamations of surprise )

977
01:15:18,139 --> 01:15:20,107
" Curfew is at 1800 hours .

978
01:15:20,975 --> 01:15:25,526
" Any persons on the street or outside their quarters after 6 : 00 p.m ...

979
01:15:26,147 --> 01:15:28,616
" ... will be subject to arrest by military police . "

980
01:15:28,816 --> 01:15:31,740
Now as for the reasons for this most drastic decision :

981
01:15:32,903 --> 01:15:37,033
A couple of months ago in the New Mexico desert , giant ants were discovered .

982
01:15:37,158 --> 01:15:42,506
They 're similar in appearance to the ones you 're familiar with .

983
01:15:43,080 --> 01:15:47,961
Except they are mutations , ranging in size from 9 to 12 feet in length .

984
01:15:48,586 --> 01:15:52,136
The New Mexico colony was destroyed , but two queen ants escaped .

985
01:15:52,381 --> 01:15:56,431
One has been found and destroyed . The other has not yet been found .

986
01:15:57,178 --> 01:16:03,311
It has established a nest in the storm drains beneath the streets of Los Angeles .

987
01:16:03,434 --> 01:16:06,734
It 's not known how long this nest has been established

988
01:16:06,979 --> 01:16:09,949
or how many of these lethal monsters have hatched .

989
01:16:10,274 --> 01:16:13,118
Maybe a few , maybe thousands .

990
01:16:14,028 --> 01:16:16,827
If new queen ants have hatched and escaped this nest

991
01:16:17,364 --> 01:16:20,834
other American cities may be in danger .

992
01:16:21,368 --> 01:16:23,621
These creatures are extremely dangerous .

993
01:16:24,497 --> 01:16:26,716
They 've already killed a number of persons .

994
01:16:26,791 --> 01:16:30,261
Stay in your homes . I repeat , stay in your homes !

995
01:16:30,836 --> 01:16:33,806
Your personal safety , the safety of the entire city

996
01:16:34,465 --> 01:16:37,890
depends upon your full cooperation with the military authorities .

997
01:16:37,968 --> 01:16:41,598
( Dramatic instrumental music )

998
01:17:00,825 --> 01:17:02,953
You got a pass to be down here , lady ?

999
01:17:03,035 --> 01:17:06,630
- No , but I 'm with Mrs. Lodge . - This is a restricted area . Let 's go .

1000
01:17:06,705 --> 01:17:07,831
Hold it , Sergeant !

1001
01:17:08,165 --> 01:17:10,088
- This is the mother- - - They have no pass- -

1002
01:17:10,167 --> 01:17:12,386
Go talk to the general .

1003
01:17:14,338 --> 01:17:15,885
BEN : Good evening , Mrs. Lodge .

1004
01:17:17,550 --> 01:17:19,427
- Is there any word yet ? - No , not yet .

1005
01:17:19,510 --> 01:17:22,138
We 've got an awful lot of people to help find them .

1006
01:17:22,263 --> 01:17:25,767
- This may take awhile . Why not go home ? - Oh , no .

1007
01:17:26,225 --> 01:17:30,355
- I want to be here when- - - Sure . Take it easy and try not to worry .

1008
01:17:36,610 --> 01:17:38,954
ENGINEER : Since time is of the essence

1009
01:17:39,029 --> 01:17:42,033
I recommend we pour gasoline into those drains and light it .

1010
01:17:42,116 --> 01:17:45,245
It 'll burn out anything in there and we can still control the fire

1011
01:17:45,327 --> 01:17:47,876
so there 'll be no property damage on the street .

1012
01:17:47,955 --> 01:17:50,674
Any ants that get through , the troops can take care of .

1013
01:17:50,749 --> 01:17:54,879
We can 't do that until we know whether those two kids are in there .

1014
01:17:54,962 --> 01:17:57,260
Think there 's a chance they 're still alive ?

1015
01:17:57,464 --> 01:18:00,809
Are we supposed to jeopardize the lives of everyone for children

1016
01:18:00,885 --> 01:18:02,808
who in all probability are already dead ?

1017
01:18:02,887 --> 01:18:06,232
- Ask their mother that question . - She 's right over there .

1018
01:18:12,605 --> 01:18:13,982
I see what you mean .

1019
01:18:14,064 --> 01:18:17,159
We not only have her to think of , but as I told you before

1020
01:18:17,234 --> 01:18:20,784
we can 't risk fire until we know if any new queens have hatched

1021
01:18:20,863 --> 01:18:23,912
and flown out of this nest . Where 's Gen. O 'Brien ?

1022
01:18:24,074 --> 01:18:26,543
- He 's over there by the command car . - Thank you .

1023
01:18:27,786 --> 01:18:30,039
- Can we start now , General ? - I think so .

1024
01:18:30,247 --> 01:18:33,467
- How about it , Major ? - Waiting for more coverage to the north .

1025
01:18:33,584 --> 01:18:35,882
Contact the northern units , soldier .

1026
01:18:36,212 --> 01:18:39,557
- Northern units come in . - How about the south ?

1027
01:18:39,673 --> 01:18:41,425
All drains as far as Long Beach

1028
01:18:41,508 --> 01:18:43,510
are covered by bazookas or flamethrowers .

1029
01:18:43,594 --> 01:18:46,393
- Openings of these drains ? - Police and Marines are covering .

1030
01:18:46,472 --> 01:18:48,019
How about it , soldier ?

1031
01:18:48,307 --> 01:18:50,401
SOLDIER : Can 't contact northern units , sir .

1032
01:18:50,851 --> 01:18:52,694
GENERAL : Let 's go ahead anyway .

1033
01:18:52,937 --> 01:18:56,316
Gen. O 'Brien to all search units : Proceed into storm drains !

1034
01:18:58,525 --> 01:19:00,448
- O 'CONNELL : Yes , sir ? - GENERAL : Get moving .

1035
01:19:00,527 --> 01:19:02,825
O 'CONNELL : Come on , boys , let 's get rolling !

1036
01:19:02,905 --> 01:19:04,498
Roll them out of here !

1037
01:19:04,573 --> 01:19:09,670
( Dramatic instrumental music )

1038
01:19:13,916 --> 01:19:15,668
Watch yourself , Bob .

1039
01:20:52,306 --> 01:20:53,899
Graham in drain 203 .

1040
01:20:54,183 --> 01:20:58,529
Graham in drain 203 . In six-tenths of a mile , nothing to report . Over .

1041
01:20:59,229 --> 01:21:00,731
Medford in drain 207 .

1042
01:21:00,814 --> 01:21:04,864
Medford in drain 207 . In half of a mile . Nothing to report , over .

1043
01:21:05,152 --> 01:21:06,620
Peterson in drain 223 .

1044
01:21:06,695 --> 01:21:10,950
Peterson in 223 , we 're in six-tenths of a mile . Nothing to report , over .

1045
01:21:11,241 --> 01:21:12,868
KIBBEE : This is Kibbee in drain 192 .

1046
01:21:12,951 --> 01:21:17,673
Repeat , Kibbee in 192 , in eight-tenths . Nothing to report , over .

1047
01:21:19,666 --> 01:21:22,670
( Rumbling )

1048
01:21:22,753 --> 01:21:24,426
Wait a minute , hold it .

1049
01:21:25,130 --> 01:21:26,473
Kill the motor .

1050
01:21:27,383 --> 01:21:31,854
( Creaking )

1051
01:21:32,262 --> 01:21:33,935
- Did you hear that ? - Yeah .

1052
01:21:36,308 --> 01:21:38,686
This is Peterson ! Stop all motors !

1053
01:21:39,353 --> 01:21:42,323
This is Peterson ! Stop all motors !

1054
01:21:45,526 --> 01:21:49,997
( Strange tapping in pipes )

1055
01:22:01,542 --> 01:22:03,419
This is Peterson in drain 223 .

1056
01:22:03,502 --> 01:22:07,382
Peterson in drain 223 . We 're in just over a mile . I hear something .

1057
01:22:10,801 --> 01:22:12,474
( Tapping in pipes )

1058
01:22:12,553 --> 01:22:14,521
There it is again . Stand by .

1059
01:22:23,856 --> 01:22:25,699
Where does this thing go ?

1060
01:22:30,028 --> 01:22:33,703
DRIVER : That pipe runs into a main line drain that isn 't finished yet .

1061
01:22:33,782 --> 01:22:35,580
Still in the construction stage .

1062
01:22:40,873 --> 01:22:42,420
BEN : Give me a hand .

1063
01:22:47,880 --> 01:22:49,427
Tell them where I 'm going .

1064
01:22:51,633 --> 01:22:55,388
Peterson is going through the connecting feeder to drain 267 .

1065
01:22:55,679 --> 01:23:00,150
We 've heard what may be the kids . Repeat , we 've heard what may be the kids .

1066
01:23:00,476 --> 01:23:01,523
Stand by .

1067
01:23:03,896 --> 01:23:06,274
- BEN : There 's construction down there ? - DRIVER : Yeah .

1068
01:23:06,356 --> 01:23:10,281
- Tell O 'Brien to turn the work lights on . - Right .

1069
01:23:11,945 --> 01:23:15,074
My map shows a portion of drain 267 is unfinished

1070
01:23:15,157 --> 01:23:18,161
with construction postponed for the last 60 days .

1071
01:23:18,327 --> 01:23:23,299
If they 've left work lights installed , turn them on . Stand by .

1072
01:23:29,630 --> 01:23:33,260
( Banging )

1073
01:23:48,982 --> 01:23:52,612
( Banging )

1074
01:23:53,612 --> 01:23:57,037
Mike ? Jerry ? Are you there ?

1075
01:23:57,115 --> 01:24:00,210
- MIKE : Yes , we 're here ! - BEN : Schmitty , they 're alive !

1076
01:24:00,285 --> 01:24:01,252
They 're alive .

1077
01:24:01,453 --> 01:24:03,672
Tell Mrs. Lodge her boys are alive .

1078
01:24:05,832 --> 01:24:09,462
( High-pitched stridulation )

1079
01:24:16,802 --> 01:24:21,649
BEN : Mike , Jerry , stay where you are ! We 'll get you out , but don 't move !

1080
01:24:22,182 --> 01:24:23,934
BEN : There 's two ants in here .

1081
01:24:24,059 --> 01:24:27,859
I got a strong brood odor , like in the New Mexico nest !

1082
01:24:28,313 --> 01:24:32,534
Report that to O 'Brien . Tell him I must be near the nest .

1083
01:24:32,609 --> 01:24:36,159
I can 't use the flamethrower . The kids are right in the line of fire .

1084
01:24:36,238 --> 01:24:38,206
BEN : Tell O 'Brien to send in troops .

1085
01:24:46,623 --> 01:24:50,093
DRIVER : Peterson says it has the same smell as the nest in New Mexico .

1086
01:24:50,168 --> 01:24:53,638
" Brood odor , " he calls it . He asks for troops to be sent in .

1087
01:24:53,797 --> 01:24:55,470
He 's found the nest !

1088
01:24:55,674 --> 01:25:00,020
To all units , condition red . Drain 267 is the target area !

1089
01:25:00,095 --> 01:25:03,190
Repeat , condition red . Drain 267 is the target area !

1090
01:25:03,265 --> 01:25:07,941
( Message repeating on radios )

1091
01:25:18,238 --> 01:25:23,335
( Dramatic instrumental music )

1092
01:25:38,925 --> 01:25:41,895
Repeat , condition red . Drain 267 is the target area .

1093
01:25:41,970 --> 01:25:45,520
O 'Connors , bring up my jeep . I hope we 've found this nest in time .

1094
01:25:49,770 --> 01:25:53,400
( High-pitched stridulation )

1095
01:26:16,463 --> 01:26:18,261
BEN : Mike , Jerry , get in the corner !

1096
01:26:30,102 --> 01:26:32,480
BEN : Come on Jerry , Mike , let 's get out of here !

1097
01:26:34,398 --> 01:26:35,820
Come on , Mike .

1098
01:26:37,025 --> 01:26:40,871
We 're going through this pipe . There 's a man at the other end .

1099
01:26:40,946 --> 01:26:44,200
Keep crawling until you get down there . Understand ?

1100
01:26:44,574 --> 01:26:46,872
BEN : Grab hold . Go on .

1101
01:26:47,577 --> 01:26:49,705
BEN : Keep crawling , to the other end .

1102
01:27:18,734 --> 01:27:20,702
( High-pitched stridulation continues )

1103
01:27:20,777 --> 01:27:22,495
GRAHAM : Put your light over there !

1104
01:27:32,247 --> 01:27:33,544
Keep at them !

1105
01:27:40,756 --> 01:27:41,803
GRAHAM : Ben .

1106
01:27:44,426 --> 01:27:47,100
- How about the kids , Ben ? - They 're okay .

1107
01:27:48,430 --> 01:27:49,477
The pipe ...

1108
01:27:52,893 --> 01:27:54,190
Medics !

1109
01:28:33,767 --> 01:28:36,486
- Stop the firing ! - Cease fire !

1110
01:28:36,561 --> 01:28:39,360
No more explosives , we can 't risk closing off the nest .

1111
01:28:39,439 --> 01:28:41,237
Is there any type of gas we can use ?

1112
01:28:41,358 --> 01:28:43,781
We can 't take a chance , might poison the whole city .

1113
01:28:43,860 --> 01:28:48,240
We must locate the egg chamber , find out if any new queens have hatched .

1114
01:28:57,332 --> 01:28:59,300
( High-pitched stridulation stops )

1115
01:29:08,301 --> 01:29:09,769
Medics !

1116
01:29:19,646 --> 01:29:24,527
( Suspenseful instrumental music )

1117
01:29:33,618 --> 01:29:35,245
GENERAL : Start digging , you guys .

1118
01:29:43,086 --> 01:29:45,054
GENERAL : Hurry up , dig .

1119
01:30:03,899 --> 01:30:08,780
( High-pitched stridulation )

1120
01:30:45,357 --> 01:30:47,576
( High-pitched stridulation stops )

1121
01:30:49,319 --> 01:30:53,790
( High-pitched stridulation )

1122
01:31:02,165 --> 01:31:04,793
Hold it . Don 't burn anything until we get the okay .

1123
01:31:04,876 --> 01:31:07,129
- General , where 's Dr. Medford ? - He 's coming .

1124
01:31:16,805 --> 01:31:18,182
Is this it , Doctor ?

1125
01:31:19,182 --> 01:31:21,435
DR. MEDFORD : New princess ants . New queens .

1126
01:31:23,019 --> 01:31:27,274
This is the egg chamber . The same as we found in New Mexico .

1127
01:31:29,067 --> 01:31:30,489
GRAHAM : Are we too late ?

1128
01:31:30,986 --> 01:31:32,738
Fortunately , we 're in time .

1129
01:31:32,904 --> 01:31:35,748
I 'm certain no new queens have escaped from this nest .

1130
01:31:35,991 --> 01:31:38,494
The job will be done when these are destroyed .

1131
01:31:38,910 --> 01:31:40,253
Okay , burn them out .

1132
01:31:47,669 --> 01:31:52,095
Pat , if these monsters are a result of the first atomic bomb in 1945

1133
01:31:52,507 --> 01:31:55,260
what about all the others that have been exploded since then ?

1134
01:31:55,343 --> 01:31:56,390
I don 't know .

1135
01:31:56,761 --> 01:31:58,308
Nobody knows , Robert .

1136
01:31:59,389 --> 01:32:03,769
When man entered the atomic age , he opened a door into a new world .

1137
01:32:04,853 --> 01:32:09,108
What we 'll eventually find in that new world , nobody can predict .

1138
01:32:10,233 --> 01:32:14,488
( Dramatic instrumental climax )

1139
01:32:26,458 --> 01:32:28,506
( English SDH )

